PathwayData.put("data/reading_writing/units/L04U2.json",{"strand":"reading_writing","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":2,"theme":"Water: Precious and Powerful","essential_question":"Why is water so important, and how can we save it?","schema_version":"1.0","core_words":["river","well","oasis","drop","flow","freeze","melt","steam","waste","save","tap","thirsty","pure","cycle"],"recycled_words":["water","desert","rain","cloud","because","so","main idea","heading","poem","palm tree","camel","first","finally"],"rubrics":[{"id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","title":"Analytic writing rubric","traits":[{"name":"Ideas","name_ar":"الأفكار","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear, interesting and fully developed with strong details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة وممتعة ومدعومة بتفاصيل قوية."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear and have enough details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة ومعها تفاصيل كافية."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"My main idea is there but needs more details.","descriptor_ar":"فكرتي الرئيسية موجودة لكنها تحتاج إلى تفاصيل أكثر."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"My ideas are unclear or very few.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري غير واضحة أو قليلة جدًا."}]},{"name":"Organization","name_ar":"التنظيم","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Clear beginning, middle and end; ideas flow with linking words.","descriptor_ar":"بداية ووسط ونهاية واضحة، والأفكار مترابطة بكلمات الربط."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Clear order with some linking words.","descriptor_ar":"ترتيب واضح مع بعض كلمات الربط."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Some order, but parts are mixed up.","descriptor_ar":"يوجد بعض الترتيب لكن بعض الأجزاء غير مرتبة."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Ideas are not in order.","descriptor_ar":"الأفكار غير مرتبة."}]},{"name":"Vocabulary","name_ar":"المفردات","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"I use exact, varied words, including new unit words, correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات دقيقة ومتنوعة، منها كلمات الوحدة الجديدة، بشكل صحيح."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"I use some new words correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم بعض الكلمات الجديدة بشكل صحيح."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"I use simple words; some are repeated or wrong.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات بسيطة، وبعضها مكرر أو غير صحيح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"I use very few words; the meaning is hard to understand.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات قليلة جدًا ويصعب فهم المعنى."}]},{"name":"Sentence fluency","name_ar":"سلاسة الجمل","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My sentences are complete, varied in length and easy to read aloud.","descriptor_ar":"جملي كاملة ومتنوعة الطول وسهلة القراءة بصوت عالٍ."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Most sentences are complete, with some variety.","descriptor_ar":"معظم جملي كاملة مع بعض التنويع."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Many sentences are short or start the same way.","descriptor_ar":"كثير من جملي قصيرة أو تبدأ بالطريقة نفسها."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Sentences are incomplete or run together.","descriptor_ar":"جملي ناقصة أو متداخلة."}]},{"name":"Conventions","name_ar":"قواعد الكتابة","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Capitals, punctuation, spelling and grammar are almost always correct.","descriptor_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة وعلامات الترقيم والإملاء والقواعد صحيحة دائمًا تقريبًا."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"A few mistakes that do not affect meaning.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء قليلة لا تؤثر في المعنى."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Several mistakes; the meaning is sometimes unclear.","descriptor_ar":"عدة أخطاء، والمعنى أحيانًا غير واضح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Many mistakes make it hard to read.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء كثيرة تجعل القراءة صعبة."}]}]}],"lessons":[{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS1","title":"Word Power: Water: Precious and Powerful","lesson_type":"vocabulary","objectives":["read, say and use 14 words about water and 3 Tier 2 words (source, conserve, result)","build word families from one base word (freeze → frozen, freezer, freezing)","describe how water changes: freeze, melt, flow and turn into steam"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة ونطق واستخدام 14 كلمة عن الماء و3 كلمات أكاديمية (source, conserve, result).","بناء عائلات الكلمات من كلمة أساسية واحدة.","وصف كيف يتغير الماء: يتجمد، يذوب، يجري، يتحول إلى بخار."],"success_criteria":["I can read and use the water words in sentences.","I can build and explain a word family.","I can say how water changes from ice to water to steam."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع قراءة كلمات الماء واستخدامها في جمل.","أستطيع بناء عائلة كلمات وشرحها.","أستطيع قول كيف يتغير الماء من جليد إلى ماء إلى بخار."],"map_area":"Vocabulary: Acquisition and Use","vocabulary":[{"word":"river","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɪvər/","definition":"a long line of water that flows to the sea","arabic":"نهر","example":"The Nile is a very long river.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"well","pos":"noun","ipa":"/wɛl/","definition":"a deep hole in the ground for getting water","arabic":"بئر","example":"The village had an old well.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"oasis","pos":"noun","ipa":"/oʊˈeɪsɪs/","definition":"a green place in the desert with water","arabic":"واحة","example":"Al-Ahsa is a famous oasis.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"drop","pos":"noun","ipa":"/drɑp/","definition":"a very small amount of liquid in a round shape","arabic":"قطرة","example":"Every drop of water is precious.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"flow","pos":"verb","ipa":"/floʊ/","definition":"to move along smoothly, like water","arabic":"يجري / يتدفق","example":"Water flows down the mountain.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"freeze","pos":"verb","ipa":"/friz/","definition":"to become hard and cold, like ice (past: froze; frozen)","arabic":"يتجمد","example":"Water freezes at 0 °C.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"melt","pos":"verb","ipa":"/mɛlt/","definition":"to change from solid to liquid because of heat","arabic":"يذوب","example":"Ice melts in the sun.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V07","tier":"core"},{"word":"steam","pos":"noun","ipa":"/stim/","definition":"the hot gas that comes from boiling water","arabic":"بخار","example":"Steam rises from the kettle.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V08","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V08","tier":"core"},{"word":"waste","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/weɪst/","definition":"to use more than you need; things or water that are used badly","arabic":"يهدر / هدر","example":"Don't waste water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V09","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V09","tier":"core"},{"word":"save","pos":"verb","ipa":"/seɪv/","definition":"to keep something so you do not lose or waste it","arabic":"يوفّر / يحفظ","example":"Turn off the tap to save water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V10","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V10","tier":"core"},{"word":"tap","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tæp/","definition":"the thing you turn to get water from a pipe","arabic":"صنبور","example":"Turn off the tap when you brush your teeth.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V11","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V11","tier":"core"},{"word":"thirsty","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈθɝsti/","definition":"needing to drink","arabic":"عطشان","example":"After football, I am very thirsty.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V12","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V12","tier":"core"},{"word":"pure","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/pjʊr/","definition":"clean, with nothing else mixed in","arabic":"نقي","example":"Pure water is safe to drink.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V13","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V13","tier":"core"},{"word":"cycle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsaɪkəl/","definition":"a set of events that happen again and again in the same order","arabic":"دورة","example":"The water cycle never stops.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V14","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V14","tier":"core"},{"word":"source","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɔrs/","definition":"where something comes from","arabic":"مصدر","example":"The sea is a source of drinking water in Saudi Arabia.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V15","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V15","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"conserve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈsɝv/","definition":"to use carefully so it lasts","arabic":"يحافظ على / يرشّد","example":"We must conserve water in the desert.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V16","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V16","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"result","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɪˈzʌlt/","definition":"something that happens because of something else","arabic":"نتيجة","example":"As a result, we saved 20 liters a day.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V17","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V17","tier":"tier2"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **word family** is a group of words that share the same **base word**. If you know the base word, you can understand the whole family.\n\nFamily members can be **verbs** (freeze, froze), **adjectives** (frozen, freezing), **nouns** for things or people (freezer, waster) and **-ing / -ed** forms (melting, melted). Endings like **-er, -ing, -ed, -ful, -y** change the job of the word.\n\nSteps: (1) Find the **base word**. (2) Look at the **ending** (or a new form like *froze/frozen*). (3) Ask: **Is it a thing, an action or a describing word?** (4) Check the meaning in the sentence.","examples":["**freeze** (verb) → **froze** (past) → **frozen** (adjective: *frozen juice*) → **freezer** (noun: a machine that freezes food) → **freezing** (very cold).","**melt** → **melted, melting**: *The melting ice made a puddle.*","**flow** → **flowing, flowed**: *The flowing water turned the wheel.*","**waste** → **wasteful** (using too much): *Long showers are wasteful.*","**save** → **saving, saver**: *A water saver uses a bucket, not a hose.*","**thirst** (noun) → **thirsty** (adjective): *The camel's thirst was great; it was very thirsty.*","**pure** → **purify** (make pure) → **purification**: *Plants purify sea water.*","**cycle** → **recycle** (use again): *We recycle plastic bottles.*","**steam** → **steamy**: *The bathroom was steamy after the shower.*"],"common_errors":["✗ The water freezed. → ✓ The water froze. (Irregular past: freeze → **froze**; adjective **frozen**.)","✗ I put the juice in the freeze. → ✓ I put the juice in the freezer. (**freezer** = the machine.)","✗ It is freezed outside. → ✓ It is freezing outside. (Very cold weather = **freezing**.)","✗ The ice is melt. → ✓ The ice is melting. / The ice melted. (Use **-ing** or **-ed**.)","✗ Don't waist water. → ✓ Don't waste water. (**waist** is part of your body!)","✗ We save water for not waste it. → ✓ We save water so we do not waste it. (Use **so** for a purpose/result.)","✗ Pure water are safe. → ✓ Pure water is safe. (Water (uncountable) → **is**.)"],"arabic":"عائلة الكلمات مجموعة كلمات تشترك في الكلمة الأساسية نفسها؛ إذا عرفت الأساس فهمت العائلة كلها.\n\nقد يكون أفراد العائلة أفعالًا (freeze, froze) أو صفات (frozen, freezing) أو أسماء (freezer) أو صيغ -ing/-ed.\n\nالخطوات: جِد الكلمة الأساسية، وانظر إلى النهاية، واسأل: هل هي شيء أم فعل أم صفة؟ ثم تحقق من المعنى في الجملة.\n\nانتبه: الماضي من freeze هو froze والصفة frozen، وwaste (يهدر) تختلف عن waist (الخصر)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hello! I am Qatra, a little drop of water. Follow my journey!","on_screen":"Water: Precious and Powerful 💧","visual":"A smiling water drop jumps out of a tap."},{"time":"00:20–01:00","narration":"I live in rivers, wells and the oasis. I flow, I freeze, I melt and I become steam!","on_screen":"river · well · oasis · drop · flow · freeze · melt · steam","visual":"Qatra flows in a river, freezes into ice, melts and rises as steam."},{"time":"01:00–01:30","narration":"Thirsty? Drink pure water! Turn off the tap – don't waste me; save me!","on_screen":"thirsty · pure · tap · waste · save","visual":"A child turns off a running tap; Qatra cheers."},{"time":"01:30–02:30","narration":"Word families: freeze, froze, frozen, freezer, freezing! One base word, many family members.","on_screen":"Word family tree 🌳","visual":"A family tree with 'freeze' on the trunk."},{"time":"02:30–03:00","narration":"The water cycle goes round and round. The sea is a source of our water – we must conserve it!","on_screen":"cycle · source · conserve · result","visual":"A circle of arrows from the sea to clouds to rain."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا! أنا قطرة ماء صغيرة. تابع رحلتي!","أعيش في الأنهار والآبار والواحات. أجري وأتجمد وأذوب وأصير بخارًا!","عطشان؟ اشرب ماءً نقيًا! أغلق الصنبور ولا تهدرني!","عائلات الكلمات: freeze, froze, frozen, freezer, freezing!","دورة الماء مستمرة، والبحر مصدر مياهنا؛ يجب أن نحافظ عليها!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female teacher, speed 0.90. A cheerful water drop character named Qatra narrates parts."},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","instructions_ar":"اختر الكلمة الصحيحة.","items":[{"q":"A green place in the desert with water is an ___.","answer":"oasis","explanation":"Oasis.","explanation_ar":"واحة.","options":["ocean","tap","oasis","steam"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Ice cream ___s quickly in the hot sun.","answer":"melt","explanation":"Heat → melt.","explanation_ar":"يذوب.","options":["freeze","flow","melt","save"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"The hot gas from boiling water is ___.","answer":"steam","explanation":"Steam.","explanation_ar":"بخار.","options":["ice","a drop","a well","steam"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Turn off the ___ while you brush your teeth.","answer":"tap","explanation":"Tap.","explanation_ar":"الصنبور.","options":["tap","river","cycle","oasis"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"After running, Omar was very ___. He drank two glasses of water.","answer":"thirsty","explanation":"Needing to drink.","explanation_ar":"عطشان.","options":["thirsty","pure","frozen","wasteful"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Clean water with nothing else mixed in is ___.","answer":"pure","explanation":"Pure.","explanation_ar":"نقي.","options":["steamy","pure","thirsty","frozen"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS1-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Word families. Choose.","instructions_ar":"عائلات الكلمات: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which word is a machine in the *freeze* family?","answer":"freezer","explanation":"-er = thing that does it.","explanation_ar":"freezer.","options":["frozen","froze","freezing","freezer"],"dok":1,"skill":"word families","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What is the past tense of *freeze*?","answer":"froze","explanation":"Irregular.","explanation_ar":"froze.","options":["freezed","frozen","freezing","froze"],"dok":2,"skill":"word families","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*We had **frozen** juice on a hot day.* *Frozen* is ___.","answer":"an adjective that describes the juice","explanation":"Describing word.","explanation_ar":"صفة.","options":["a verb in the future","an adjective that describes the juice","a kind of machine","a noun for a person"],"dok":2,"skill":"word families","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which word means *using too much*?","answer":"wasteful","explanation":"-ful adjective.","explanation_ar":"wasteful.","options":["waste","wasted","wasteful","waster"],"dok":2,"skill":"word families","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which word belongs to the *thirst* family?","answer":"thirsty","explanation":"thirst → thirsty.","explanation_ar":"thirsty.","options":["third","thirsty","throat","thirteen"],"dok":1,"skill":"word families","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Plants that **purify** sea water help people.* *Purify* means ___.","answer":"make pure and clean","explanation":"pure → purify.","explanation_ar":"ينقّي.","options":["make pure and clean","make dirty","freeze","waste"],"dok":3,"skill":"word families","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS1-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word bank.","instructions_ar":"استخدم بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"In Saudi Arabia, the sea is an important ________ of drinking water.","answer":"source","explanation":"Where something comes from.","explanation_ar":"مصدر.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"We must ________ water because there is very little rain.","answer":"conserve","explanation":"Use carefully.","explanation_ar":"نرشّد.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"We fixed the leaking tap. As a ________, we saved water.","answer":"result","explanation":"What happens because of something.","explanation_ar":"نتيجة.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Rain, rivers and clouds are part of the water ________.","answer":"cycle","explanation":"Events that happen again and again.","explanation_ar":"دورة.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Long ago, villagers got water from a deep ________.","answer":"well","explanation":"A hole for water.","explanation_ar":"بئر.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Every ________ of water counts!","answer":"drop","explanation":"A tiny amount.","explanation_ar":"قطرة.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS1-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write with the new words.","instructions_ar":"اكتب باستخدام الكلمات الجديدة.","items":[{"q":"Write three words in the *melt* family and use one in a sentence.","answer":"melt, melted, melting – The melting snow made a small river.","explanation":"Family + sentence.","explanation_ar":"العائلة + جملة.","dok":2,"skill":"word families","stage":"production"},{"q":"Explain how water changes when it gets very cold and very hot.","answer":"When water gets very cold, it freezes into ice. When it gets very hot, it turns into steam.","explanation":"freeze + steam.","explanation_ar":"freeze + steam.","dok":2,"skill":"explain","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write one way your family wastes water and one way to save it.","answer":"We leave the tap on when we wash dishes. We can fill the sink instead.","explanation":"Waste + save.","explanation_ar":"هدر + توفير.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Why is water precious in Saudi Arabia?","answer":"Because there are no rivers and very little rain, so we must conserve every drop.","explanation":"Reason.","explanation_ar":"سبب.","dok":3,"skill":"reasoning","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Water Word Families","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Family tree: a base word grows on a trunk; the child drags endings and forms to make real family members on the branches and taps each to hear it in a sentence. Wrong words fall like dry leaves.","Teams get a base word and a pile of endings and forms.","In 3 minutes, they build as many real family members as they can on their tree.","Teams read each word and use one in a water sentence.","Other teams check that each word is real.","Each real word = 1 point; each correct sentence = 1 bonus point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which word means *where something comes from*?","answer":"source","explanation":"Source.","explanation_ar":"مصدر.","options":["result","source","cycle","drop"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which word is NOT in the *freeze* family?","answer":"free","explanation":"free is a different word.","explanation_ar":"free.","options":["free","frozen","freezer","froze"],"dok":1,"skill":"word families"},{"q":"*Don't waste water.* *Waste* means ___.","answer":"use more than you need","explanation":"Waste.","explanation_ar":"يهدر.","options":["drink","freeze","clean","use more than you need"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Water that moves smoothly along a river ___.","answer":"flows","explanation":"Flow.","explanation_ar":"يجري.","options":["freezes","melts","flows","steams"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about the cold night is correct?","answer":"The water in the bucket froze last night.","explanation":"Past: froze.","explanation_ar":"froze.","options":["The water in the bucket freezed last night.","The water in the bucket froze last night.","The water in the bucket frozen last night.","The water in the bucket freeze last night."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"*We must conserve water.* *Conserve* means ___.","answer":"use carefully so it lasts","explanation":"Conserve.","explanation_ar":"نرشّد.","options":["waste it quickly","use carefully so it lasts","freeze it","sell it"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which word describes very cold weather?","answer":"freezing","explanation":"-ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"freezing.","options":["freezing","freezer","froze","melted"],"dok":2,"skill":"word families"},{"q":"How can knowing a base word help you?","answer":"You can understand the other words in its family.","explanation":"Family meanings.","explanation_ar":"تفهم بقية أفراد العائلة.","options":["It tells you the spelling of every word.","It makes words shorter.","It only works for verbs.","You can understand the other words in its family."],"dok":2,"skill":"strategy"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *result* correctly?","answer":"We took shorter showers. As a result, our water bill went down.","explanation":"As a result + effect.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Result we took showers.","As a result, before we started.","We took shorter showers. As a result, our water bill went down.","The result is a tap."],"dok":3,"skill":"usage"},{"q":"Which action would conserve the MOST water?","answer":"fixing a tap that drips all day","explanation":"Leaks waste a lot.","explanation_ar":"إصلاح الصنبور المسرّب.","options":["fixing a tap that drips all day","drinking a glass of water","washing hands once","watering one small plant"],"dok":3,"skill":"apply"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'river': a river flowing through green land"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'well': a stone well with a bucket"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'oasis': palm trees around water in the desert"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'drop': a single water drop"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'flow': water flowing over rocks"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'freeze': an ice cube tray"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'melt': a melting ice cube"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V08","prompt":"Picture for the word 'steam': steam from a kettle"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V09","prompt":"Picture for the word 'waste': a running tap with no one using it"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V10","prompt":"Picture for the word 'save': a hand turning off a tap"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V11","prompt":"Picture for the word 'tap': a kitchen tap"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V12","prompt":"Picture for the word 'thirsty': a child drinking water after sport"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V13","prompt":"Picture for the word 'pure': a clear glass of water"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V14","prompt":"Picture for the word 'cycle': a circle of arrows: sea, cloud, rain"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V15","prompt":"Picture for the word 'source': a pipe coming from the sea to a city"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V16","prompt":"Picture for the word 'conserve': a family using a bucket instead of a hose"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V17","prompt":"Picture for the word 'result': an arrow pointing to a full water tank"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-01","prompt":"An oasis, a desalination plant and a child turning off a tap."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-02","prompt":"Water as ice, liquid and steam."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS1-03","prompt":"A word family tree for freeze."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V01","script":"river. The Nile is a very long river."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V02","script":"well. The village had an old well."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V03","script":"oasis. Al-Ahsa is a famous oasis."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V04","script":"drop. Every drop of water is precious."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V05","script":"flow. Water flows down the mountain."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V06","script":"freeze. Water freezes at 0 °C."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V07","script":"melt. Ice melts in the sun."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V08","script":"steam. Steam rises from the kettle."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V09","script":"waste. Don't waste water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V10","script":"save. Turn off the tap to save water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V11","script":"tap. Turn off the tap when you brush your teeth."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V12","script":"thirsty. After football, I am very thirsty."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V13","script":"pure. Pure water is safe to drink."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V14","script":"cycle. The water cycle never stops."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V15","script":"source. The sea is a source of drinking water in Saudi Arabia."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V16","script":"conserve. We must conserve water in the desert."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-V17","script":"result. As a result, we saved 20 liters a day."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Hello! I am Qatra, a little drop of water. Follow my journey! I live in rivers, wells and the oasis. I flow, I freeze, I melt and I become steam! Thirsty? Drink pure water! Turn off the tap – don't waste me; save me! Word families: freeze, froze, frozen, freezer, freezing! One base word, many family members. The water cycle goes round and round. The sea is a source of our water – we must conserve it!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS2","title":"Where Does Our Water Come From?","lesson_type":"close_reading","objectives":["read an informational article of about 260 words about the sources of water in Saudi Arabia","summarize each section in one sentence and the whole article in two or three sentences","answer literal, inferential and evaluative questions with evidence"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة مقال معلوماتي من نحو 290 كلمة عن مصادر المياه في السعودية.","تلخيص كل قسم في جملة واحدة والمقال كله في جملتين أو ثلاث.","الإجابة عن أسئلة حرفية واستنتاجية وتقييمية مع الدليل."],"success_criteria":["I can find the main idea of each section.","I can write a short summary with only the important ideas, in my own words.","I can explain where our water comes from with evidence."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع إيجاد الفكرة الرئيسية لكل قسم.","أستطيع كتابة ملخص قصير بالأفكار المهمة فقط وبكلماتي.","أستطيع شرح مصدر مياهنا مع الدليل."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"wonder","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈwʌndər/","definition":"to want to know about something","arabic":"يتساءل","example":"Have you ever wondered where water comes from?","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"invisible","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɪzəbəl/","definition":"not able to be seen","arabic":"غير مرئي","example":"Water vapor is invisible.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"water vapor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɔtər ˈveɪpər/","definition":"water as an invisible gas in the air","arabic":"بخار الماء","example":"The sun turns water into water vapor.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"soak","pos":"verb","ipa":"/soʊk/","definition":"to go into something and make it very wet","arabic":"يتشرّب / ينقع","example":"Rain soaks into the ground.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"groundwater","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡraʊndwɔtər/","definition":"water under the ground in rocks and sand","arabic":"المياه الجوفية","example":"Wells bring groundwater up.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"desalination","pos":"noun","ipa":"/diˌsælɪˈneɪʃən/","definition":"taking the salt out of sea water","arabic":"تحلية","example":"Desalination gives us drinking water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"summary","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsʌməri/","definition":"a short way of telling the most important ideas","arabic":"ملخص","example":"Write a summary of the article.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **summary** tells the **most important ideas** of a text in a **short** way, in **your own words**. It does not include small details, examples or your opinion.\n\nFor an article with headings, summarize **section by section**: read each section and ask **What is this part mostly about?** Write **one sentence** for each section.\n\nThen join your section sentences into a **short summary** of 2–3 sentences. Start with the **topic** of the whole article. Leave out numbers and examples unless they are very important.","examples":["Section 1 – The Water Cycle: **Water moves in a cycle: it rises as vapor, makes clouds, falls as rain and starts again.**","Section 2 – Water Under the Ground: **Saudi Arabia gets water from deep wells that bring up old groundwater.**","Section 3 – Water from the Sea: **Desalination plants remove salt from sea water to make drinking water.**","Section 4 – Why We Must Save It: **Getting water costs a lot, and groundwater refills slowly, so we must save water.**","Whole summary: **In Saudi Arabia, our water comes from deep wells and from sea water that desalination plants make safe to drink. Because getting this water is hard and expensive, everyone must use it carefully.**","Leave out: *Oases like Al-Ahsa can grow palm trees* (an example).","Leave out: *This water travels through long pipes to cities like Riyadh* (a small detail).","Own words: *invisible gas* → **a gas you cannot see**.","Not a summary: *I think desalination is cool.* (opinion)"],"common_errors":["✗ Copying whole sentences from the text. → ✓ Use your own words: 'a gas you cannot see'. (A summary is in **your words**.)","✗ Including every example and number. → ✓ Keep only the **most important** ideas. (Short and important.)","✗ Adding your opinion. → ✓ Report what the article says. (No opinions in a summary.)","✗ Summarizing only the first section. → ✓ Summarize **every** section, then join them. (Cover the whole text.)","✗ The water come from the sea. → ✓ The water comes from the sea. (Water (uncountable) → **comes**.)","✗ Saudi Arabia have no rivers. → ✓ Saudi Arabia has no rivers. (One country → **has**.)"],"arabic":"الملخص يعرض أهم أفكار النص باختصار وبكلماتك، دون التفاصيل الصغيرة أو الأمثلة أو رأيك.\n\nفي المقال ذي العناوين الفرعية لخّص قسمًا قسمًا: اسأل عمّ يتحدث هذا الجزء في الغالب؟ واكتب جملة واحدة لكل قسم.\n\nثم اجمع جمل الأقسام في ملخص قصير من جملتين أو ثلاث يبدأ بموضوع المقال كله.\n\nفي السعودية تأتي المياه من الآبار العميقة (المياه الجوفية) ومن تحلية مياه البحر."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Turn on the tap… where does the water come from? Let's follow Qatra!","on_screen":"Where Does Our Water Come From?","visual":"Qatra jumps out of a kitchen tap and travels backward through pipes."},{"time":"00:20–01:40","narration":"When you turn on the tap, clean water comes out…","on_screen":"(article, section by section)","visual":"Animated water cycle; a cutaway of groundwater under dunes and a deep well; a desalination plant and long pipes to Riyadh."},{"time":"01:40–02:20","narration":"Summarize section by section: one sentence for each heading!","on_screen":"Section → one sentence","visual":"Four headings each shrink into one short sentence card."},{"time":"02:20–02:45","narration":"Join them: Our water comes from deep wells and the sea, and we must use it carefully!","on_screen":"Short summary ✂️","visual":"Four cards merge into one summary card."},{"time":"02:45–03:00","narration":"Every drop is precious!","on_screen":"Save water 💧","visual":"Qatra waves from a closed tap."}],"captions_ar":["افتح الصنبور… من أين يأتي الماء؟ لنتبع قطرة!","عندما تفتح الصنبور يخرج ماء نظيف…","لخّص قسمًا قسمًا: جملة واحدة لكل عنوان!","اجمعها: يأتي ماؤنا من الآبار العميقة ومن البحر، ويجب أن نستخدمه بعناية!","كل قطرة ثمينة!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, documentary voice (female), speed 0.90. Qatra the water drop adds comments."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Where Does Our Water Come From?","body":"When you turn on the tap, clean water comes out. But have you ever wondered where that water comes from? In a dry country like Saudi Arabia, the answer is very interesting.\n\n**The Water Cycle**\n\nAll the water on Earth moves in a cycle. First, the sun heats water in seas and lakes, and it turns into an invisible gas called water vapor. The vapor rises into the sky, cools down and makes clouds. When the drops in the clouds get heavy, they fall as rain. The rain flows into rivers and seas or soaks into the ground. Then the cycle begins again.\n\n**Water Under the Ground**\n\nSaudi Arabia has no rivers, and it rains very little. However, under the desert there is old water that collected in the rocks thousands of years ago. People dig deep wells to pump this groundwater up. Oases like Al-Ahsa can grow palm trees because of water under the ground.\n\n**Water from the Sea**\n\nToday, much of our drinking water comes from the sea. Sea water is too salty to drink, so huge plants called desalination plants remove the salt. Saudi Arabia makes more desalinated water than almost any other country in the world. This water travels through long pipes to cities like Riyadh.\n\n**Why We Must Save It**\n\nGetting water from deep wells and from the sea takes a lot of energy and money. Groundwater also takes thousands of years to fill up again. As a result, every drop is precious, and everyone can help by using water carefully.","word_count":256,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U2-LS2-1","genre":"informational","role":"main","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[{"word":"water vapor","definition":"water as an invisible gas in the air","arabic":"بخار الماء"},{"word":"groundwater","definition":"water that is under the ground in rocks and sand","arabic":"المياه الجوفية"},{"word":"desalination plant","definition":"a big factory that removes salt from sea water","arabic":"محطة تحلية"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the article. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ المقال واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What does the sun do to water in seas and lakes?","answer":"It heats the water and turns it into water vapor.","explanation":"The Water Cycle.","explanation_ar":"يسخّنها فتتحول إلى بخار.","options":["It freezes the water.","It heats the water and turns it into water vapor.","It makes the water salty.","It pumps the water into wells."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What happens when the drops in the clouds get heavy?","answer":"They fall as rain.","explanation":"The Water Cycle.","explanation_ar":"تسقط مطرًا.","options":["They turn into salt.","They become wells.","They disappear forever.","They fall as rain."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where is the old water under the desert?","answer":"in the rocks under the ground","explanation":"Water Under the Ground.","explanation_ar":"في الصخور تحت الأرض.","options":["in the clouds","in long pipes","in the rocks under the ground","in the sea"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why can oases like Al-Ahsa grow palm trees?","answer":"There is water under the ground.","explanation":"Water Under the Ground.","explanation_ar":"لوجود مياه جوفية.","options":["It rains every day there.","There is a big river.","Desalination plants are there.","There is water under the ground."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What do desalination plants remove from sea water?","answer":"salt","explanation":"Water from the Sea.","explanation_ar":"الملح.","options":["salt","sand","fish","sugar"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why must we save water, according to the article?","answer":"Getting it takes a lot of energy and money, and groundwater refills very slowly.","explanation":"Why We Must Save It.","explanation_ar":"لأن الحصول عليه مكلف والمياه الجوفية بطيئة التجدد.","options":["Water tastes bad.","Pipes are long.","Getting it takes a lot of energy and money, and groundwater refills very slowly.","Clouds are heavy."],"dok":2,"skill":"reasons","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS2-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Summarizing. Choose.","instructions_ar":"التلخيص: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which sentence BEST summarizes *The Water Cycle* section?","answer":"Water rises as vapor, makes clouds, falls as rain and starts again.","explanation":"The whole section in one sentence.","explanation_ar":"تلخيص القسم.","options":["The sun is hot.","Clouds are white.","Water rises as vapor, makes clouds, falls as rain and starts again.","Rain soaks into the ground."],"dok":2,"skill":"summarizing","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence BEST summarizes *Water from the Sea*?","answer":"Desalination plants make sea water safe to drink.","explanation":"Main idea of the section.","explanation_ar":"تلخيص القسم.","options":["Riyadh is a big city.","Desalination plants make sea water safe to drink.","Pipes are long.","Sea water is blue."],"dok":2,"skill":"summarizing","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which detail should you LEAVE OUT of a short summary?","answer":"This water travels through long pipes to cities like Riyadh.","explanation":"A small detail.","explanation_ar":"تفصيل صغير.","options":["This water travels through long pipes to cities like Riyadh.","Much of our water comes from the sea.","Wells bring up groundwater.","We must save water."],"dok":2,"skill":"summarizing","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which is NOT a good summary sentence?","answer":"I think desalination plants are the coolest thing ever.","explanation":"Opinion.","explanation_ar":"رأي.","options":["Our water comes from wells and the sea.","I think desalination plants are the coolest thing ever.","Desalination removes salt from sea water.","We must use water carefully."],"dok":2,"skill":"summarizing","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which phrase means the same as *invisible gas* in your own words?","answer":"a gas you cannot see","explanation":"Paraphrase.","explanation_ar":"غاز لا تراه.","options":["a gas you cannot see","a heavy cloud","salty water","a deep well"],"dok":1,"skill":"paraphrasing","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which summary of the whole article is BEST?","answer":"In Saudi Arabia, our water comes from deep wells and from the sea. Because getting it is hard and expensive, we must save it.","explanation":"Short + all main ideas.","explanation_ar":"الملخص الأفضل.","options":["Saudi Arabia has no rivers.","The sun heats water. Clouds form. Rain falls. Wells are deep. Pipes are long. Salt is removed.","I like water.","In Saudi Arabia, our water comes from deep wells and from the sea. Because getting it is hard and expensive, we must save it."],"dok":3,"skill":"summarizing","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS2-A3","type":"highlight","stage":"freer","instructions":"Find the evidence: Find the evidence.","instructions_ar":"ابحث عن الدليل.","items":[{"q":"Underline the sentence that tells where much of our drinking water comes from today.","answer":"Today, much of our drinking water comes from the sea.","explanation":"Today + source.","explanation_ar":"اليوم + المصدر.","evidence":"Today, much of our drinking water comes from the sea.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U2-LS2-1","dok":1,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["When you turn on the tap, clean water comes out.","But have you ever wondered where that water comes from?","In a dry country like Saudi Arabia, the answer is very interesting.","**The Water Cycle**","All the water on Earth moves in a cycle.","First, the sun heats water in seas and lakes, and it turns into an invisible gas called water vapor.","The vapor rises into the sky, cools down and makes clouds.","When the drops in the clouds get heavy, they fall as rain.","The rain flows into rivers and seas or soaks into the ground.","Then the cycle begins again.","**Water Under the Ground**","Saudi Arabia has no rivers, and it rains very little.","However, under the desert there is old water that collected in the rocks thousands of years ago.","People dig deep wells to pump this groundwater up.","Oases like Al-Ahsa can grow palm trees because of water under the ground.","**Water from the Sea**","Today, much of our drinking water comes from the sea.","Sea water is too salty to drink, so huge plants called desalination plants remove the salt.","Saudi Arabia makes more desalinated water than almost any other country in the world.","This water travels through long pipes to cities like Riyadh.","**Why We Must Save It**","Getting water from deep wells and from the sea takes a lot of energy and money.","Groundwater also takes thousands of years to fill up again.","As a result, every drop is precious, and everyone can help by using water carefully."]},{"q":"Underline the sentence that explains why groundwater is precious.","answer":"Groundwater also takes thousands of years to fill up again.","explanation":"Slow refill.","explanation_ar":"بطيئة التجدد.","evidence":"Groundwater also takes thousands of years to fill up again.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U2-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["When you turn on the tap, clean water comes out.","But have you ever wondered where that water comes from?","In a dry country like Saudi Arabia, the answer is very interesting.","**The Water Cycle**","All the water on Earth moves in a cycle.","First, the sun heats water in seas and lakes, and it turns into an invisible gas called water vapor.","The vapor rises into the sky, cools down and makes clouds.","When the drops in the clouds get heavy, they fall as rain.","The rain flows into rivers and seas or soaks into the ground.","Then the cycle begins again.","**Water Under the Ground**","Saudi Arabia has no rivers, and it rains very little.","However, under the desert there is old water that collected in the rocks thousands of years ago.","People dig deep wells to pump this groundwater up.","Oases like Al-Ahsa can grow palm trees because of water under the ground.","**Water from the Sea**","Today, much of our drinking water comes from the sea.","Sea water is too salty to drink, so huge plants called desalination plants remove the salt.","Saudi Arabia makes more desalinated water than almost any other country in the world.","This water travels through long pipes to cities like Riyadh.","**Why We Must Save It**","Getting water from deep wells and from the sea takes a lot of energy and money.","Groundwater also takes thousands of years to fill up again.","As a result, every drop is precious, and everyone can help by using water carefully."]},{"q":"What does the word *However* show in *Saudi Arabia has no rivers… However, under the desert there is old water*?","answer":"a surprising, different idea","explanation":"However = contrast.","explanation_ar":"فكرة مختلفة مفاجئة.","options":["a list of examples","the first step","a surprising, different idea","the end of the text"],"dok":2,"skill":"signal words","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Why does the writer start with a question?","answer":"to make the reader curious and want to read on","explanation":"Hook.","explanation_ar":"لإثارة فضول القارئ.","options":["to give the answer right away","to tell a story","to list the headings","to make the reader curious and want to read on"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS2-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Summarize and explain.","instructions_ar":"لخّص واشرح.","items":[{"q":"Write a one-sentence summary of *Water Under the Ground*.","answer":"Saudi Arabia gets water from deep wells that bring up old water stored in rocks.","explanation":"One sentence.","explanation_ar":"جملة واحدة.","dok":2,"skill":"summarizing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a 2–3 sentence summary of the whole article in your own words.","answer":"Our water in Saudi Arabia comes from groundwater and from the sea. Desalination plants take out the salt. Because this is expensive, we must save water.","explanation":"Short summary.","explanation_ar":"ملخص قصير.","dok":3,"skill":"summarizing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Why do you think Saudi Arabia built so many desalination plants?","answer":"Because there are no rivers and little rain, but there is a lot of sea water.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"استنتاج.","dok":3,"skill":"inference","stage":"production"},{"q":"Which water source surprised you the most? Why?","answer":"The desalination plants, because I didn't know we drink water from the sea.","explanation":"Opinion + reason.","explanation_ar":"رأي + سبب.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS2-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"Where Does Our Water Come From?\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “Where Does Our Water Come From?”.","answer":"256 words","title":"Where Does Our Water Come From?","body":"When you turn on the tap, clean water comes out. But have you ever wondered where that water comes from? In a dry country like Saudi Arabia, the answer is very interesting.\n\n**The Water Cycle**\n\nAll the water on Earth moves in a cycle. First, the sun heats water in seas and lakes, and it turns into an invisible gas called water vapor. The vapor rises into the sky, cools down and makes clouds. When the drops in the clouds get heavy, they fall as rain. The rain flows into rivers and seas or soaks into the ground. Then the cycle begins again.\n\n**Water Under the Ground**\n\nSaudi Arabia has no rivers, and it rains very little. However, under the desert there is old water that collected in the rocks thousands of years ago. People dig deep wells to pump this groundwater up. Oases like Al-Ahsa can grow palm trees because of water under the ground.\n\n**Water from the Sea**\n\nToday, much of our drinking water comes from the sea. Sea water is too salty to drink, so huge plants called desalination plants remove the salt. Saudi Arabia makes more desalinated water than almost any other country in the world. This water travels through long pipes to cities like Riyadh.\n\n**Why We Must Save It**\n\nGetting water from deep wells and from the sea takes a lot of energy and money. Groundwater also takes thousands of years to fill up again. As a result, every drop is precious, and everyone can help by using water carefully.","words":256,"limit":195}],"time_limit_sec":195}],"game":{"name":"Summary Squeeze","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Squeeze machine: a long paragraph enters a machine; the child drags out only the key-idea words and builds a one-sentence summary under a word limit. Summaries that keep the main idea fill the water tank.","Teams get one section card.","They write a one-sentence summary of 15 words or fewer.","Teams read their sentence; others check: main idea? own words? no small details?","Shortest clear summary wins the round.","Main idea kept = 2 points; under 15 words = 1 bonus point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is *Where Does Our Water Come From?* mostly about?","answer":"the sources of water in Saudi Arabia and why we must save it","explanation":"Main topic.","explanation_ar":"مصادر المياه في السعودية.","options":["how to swim","a trip to the beach","the history of pipes","the sources of water in Saudi Arabia and why we must save it"],"dok":1,"skill":"main topic"},{"q":"A summary includes ___.","answer":"only the most important ideas","explanation":"Summary.","explanation_ar":"أهم الأفكار فقط.","options":["every detail and number","only the most important ideas","your opinion","a new story"],"dok":1,"skill":"summarizing"},{"q":"*Rain soaks into the ground.* *Soaks* means ___.","answer":"goes into and makes it wet","explanation":"Soak.","explanation_ar":"يتشرّب.","options":["freezes","goes into and makes it wet","flies up","dries out"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"What is *groundwater*?","answer":"water under the ground in rocks and sand","explanation":"Glossary.","explanation_ar":"المياه الجوفية.","options":["water in the clouds","sea water","water under the ground in rocks and sand","water in a glass"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about Saudi Arabia is correct?","answer":"Saudi Arabia has no rivers.","explanation":"has.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Saudi Arabia have no rivers.","Saudi Arabia having no rivers.","Saudi Arabia no has rivers.","Saudi Arabia has no rivers."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Why is sea water treated in desalination plants?","answer":"It is too salty to drink.","explanation":"Cause.","explanation_ar":"لأنه مالح جدًا.","options":["It is too cold.","It is too salty to drink.","It is too sweet.","It has too much sand."],"dok":1,"skill":"cause and effect"},{"q":"Which section would help you answer *How do clouds form?*","answer":"The Water Cycle","explanation":"Headings.","explanation_ar":"The Water Cycle.","options":["The Water Cycle","Water from the Sea","Why We Must Save It","Water Under the Ground"],"dok":2,"skill":"text features"},{"q":"Which is the BEST one-sentence summary of the article?","answer":"Our water comes from deep wells and the sea, and we must use it carefully.","explanation":"Short + main ideas.","explanation_ar":"الملخص الأفضل.","options":["The sun heats the sea.","Al-Ahsa has palm trees.","Our water comes from deep wells and the sea, and we must use it carefully.","Riyadh has long pipes."],"dok":3,"skill":"summarizing"},{"q":"What can you infer about water in Saudi Arabia from the last section?","answer":"Wasting water costs the country energy and money.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"الهدر يكلّف الطاقة والمال.","options":["Wasting water costs the country energy and money.","Water is free and endless.","It rains a lot in Riyadh.","Groundwater refills every week."],"dok":3,"skill":"inference"},{"q":"Why should a summary be in your own words?","answer":"It shows you understand and is not copying.","explanation":"Own words.","explanation_ar":"ليُظهر فهمك ولا يكون نسخًا.","options":["It makes it longer.","It changes the facts.","It shows you understand and is not copying.","It adds your opinion."],"dok":2,"skill":"summarizing"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'wonder': a child with a question mark looking at a tap"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'invisible': a dotted outline of steam disappearing"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'water vapor': arrows rising from the sea"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'soak': water soaking into sand"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'groundwater': a cutaway of water in rocks under the desert"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'desalination': a large desalination plant by the sea"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'summary': a long page shrinking into a small card"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-01","prompt":"A labelled water cycle diagram."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-02","prompt":"A cutaway of groundwater under the desert and a deep well."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS2-03","prompt":"A desalination plant with pipes to a city."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V01","script":"wonder. Have you ever wondered where water comes from?"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V02","script":"invisible. Water vapor is invisible."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V03","script":"water vapor. The sun turns water into water vapor."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V04","script":"soak. Rain soaks into the ground."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V05","script":"groundwater. Wells bring groundwater up."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V06","script":"desalination. Desalination gives us drinking water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-V07","script":"summary. Write a summary of the article."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-T1","script":"When you turn on the tap, clean water comes out. But have you ever wondered where that water comes from? In a dry country like Saudi Arabia, the answer is very interesting. **The Water Cycle** All the water on Earth moves in a cycle. First, the sun heats water in seas and lakes, and it turns into an invisible gas called water vapor. The vapor rises into the sky, cools down and makes clouds. When the drops in the clouds get heavy, they fall as rain. The rain flows into rivers and seas or soaks into the ground. Then the cycle begins again. **Water Under the Ground** Saudi Arabia has no rivers, and it rains very little. However, under the desert there is old water that collected in the rocks thousands of years ago. People dig deep wells to pump this groundwater up. Oases like Al-Ahsa can grow palm trees because of water under the ground. **Water from the Sea** Today, much of our drinking water comes from the sea. Sea water is too salty to drink, so huge plants called desalination plants remove the salt. Saudi Arabia makes more desalinated water than almost any other country in the world. This water travels through long pipes to cities like Riyadh. **Why We Must Save It** Getting water from deep wells and from the sea takes a lot of energy and money. Groundwater also takes thousands of years to fill up again. As a result, every drop is precious, and everyone can help by using water carefully."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS2-VID","script":"Turn on the tap… where does the water come from? Let's follow Qatra! When you turn on the tap, clean water comes out… Summarize section by section: one sentence for each heading! Join them: Our water comes from deep wells and the sea, and we must use it carefully! Every drop is precious!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS3","title":"Cause and effect: \"The Song of the Well\"","lesson_type":"strategy_paired_text","objectives":["find causes and effects in a poem and an article about water","use signal words (because, so, as a result, if … then) to find what happened and why","complete a Cause → Effect Chain and compare how the poem and the article give the same message"],"objectives_ar":["إيجاد الأسباب والنتائج في قصيدة ومقال عن الماء.","استخدام كلمات الإشارة لإيجاد ما حدث ولماذا.","إكمال سلسلة السبب ← النتيجة ومقارنة كيف يوصل النصان الرسالة نفسها."],"success_criteria":["I can say what happened (effect) and why it happened (cause).","I can find signal words for cause and effect.","I can show how one effect becomes the next cause in a chain."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع قول ما حدث (النتيجة) ولماذا حدث (السبب).","أستطيع إيجاد كلمات الإشارة للسبب والنتيجة.","أستطيع إظهار كيف تصبح النتيجة سببًا جديدًا في سلسلة."],"map_area":"Literary Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"silence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsaɪləns/","definition":"no sound at all","arabic":"صمت","example":"The well waited in silence.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"traveler","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtrævələr/","definition":"a person who goes on a journey","arabic":"مسافر","example":"The travelers stopped at the oasis.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"bucket","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbʌkɪt/","definition":"an open container with a handle for carrying water","arabic":"دلو","example":"He lowered the bucket into the well.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"pump","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/pʌmp/","definition":"a machine that pushes or pulls water up; to move water with a machine","arabic":"مضخة / يضخ","example":"The pump pulls water from deep under the ground.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"flood","pos":"verb","ipa":"/flʌd/","definition":"to cover with too much water","arabic":"يُغرق / يفيض","example":"They flooded the garden with water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"whisper","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/ˈwɪspər/","definition":"a very quiet voice; to speak very quietly","arabic":"همس / يهمس","example":"My voice is a whisper.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"rarely","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈrɛrli/","definition":"not often","arabic":"نادرًا","example":"Rain rarely falls in the desert.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"An **effect** is **what happened**. A **cause** is **why it happened**. Ask: **What happened? → effect. Why did it happen? → cause.**\n\n**Signal words** help you find them: **because, since** (the cause comes next); **so, as a result, that is why** (the effect comes next); **if … (then)** (a possible effect).\n\nSometimes there is a **chain**: one effect becomes the **cause** of the next thing. Pumps took too much water → the water level went down → the well became low → it may dry up. Poems and articles can show the same chain in different ways.","examples":["*Camels came, thirsty and tired, **because** the hot sun had burned all the day.* Cause: **the hot sun**. Effect: **the camels were thirsty and tired**.","*The travelers lowered their buckets, **so** they could drink.* Cause: **they lowered the buckets**. Effect: **they could drink**.","*People let taps run, … **and so** my deep water slowly slipped away.* Cause: **people wasted water**. Effect: **the water went away**.","*If you keep wasting, my song will stop.* Possible cause: **wasting water**. Possible effect: **the well dries up**.","Article: *Sea water is too salty to drink, **so** huge plants remove the salt.* Cause: **too salty**. Effect: **desalination plants**.","Article: *Getting water … takes a lot of energy and money. **As a result**, every drop is precious.*","No signal word: *Rain rarely visits; the rocks fill so slowly.* Cause: **little rain**. Effect: **the rocks fill slowly**.","Chain: **pumps work night and day** → **the water level drops** → **the well is a whisper** → **the song may stop**.","Same message, two texts: the **article** gives **facts**; the **poem** lets the **well speak** and shows **feelings**. Both say: **save water**."],"common_errors":["✗ Mixing up cause and effect. → ✓ Ask 'What happened?' for the effect first. (Effect = what; cause = why.)","✗ Thinking every cause has a signal word. → ✓ Look for causes without signal words too. (Some causes are hidden.)","✗ Because the sun was hot. → ✓ The camels were thirsty because the sun was hot. (A **because** part needs a main sentence.)","✗ The pumps worked so the water go down. → ✓ The pumps worked, so the water went down. (Past tense: **went**.)","✗ The well is speak. → ✓ The well speaks. (Present simple: **speaks**.)","✗ If you will waste water, the well dries up. → ✓ If you waste water, the well will dry up. (**If** + present → **will** + verb.)"],"arabic":"النتيجة هي ما حدث، والسبب هو لماذا حدث. اسأل: ماذا حدث؟ ← النتيجة. لماذا حدث؟ ← السبب.\n\nكلمات الإشارة: because/since يأتي بعدها السبب؛ so/as a result يأتي بعدها النتيجة؛ if… then نتيجة محتملة.\n\nأحيانًا توجد سلسلة: تصبح النتيجة سببًا لشيء جديد، مثل: ضخّ كثير ← انخفاض الماء ← ضعف البئر ← قد تجفّ.\n\nالمقال يعطي حقائق، والقصيدة تجعل البئر يتكلم وتُظهر المشاعر، وكلاهما يقول: وفّر الماء."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Listen… the old well is singing. What is its song about?","on_screen":"The Song of the Well 🎵","visual":"An old stone well in an oasis at sunset; a soft echo sound."},{"time":"00:20–01:30","narration":"I am the well in the old oasis…","on_screen":"(poem, stanza by stanza)","visual":"Camels and travelers with buckets; loud pumps; flooded gardens; the water level dropping inside a cutaway of the well."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"What happened? That's the effect. Why? That's the cause!","on_screen":"Cause → Effect","visual":"Arrows link 'pumps work night and day' to 'the water slips away'."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"One effect can cause the next thing: a chain!","on_screen":"Cause → Effect Chain 🔗","visual":"A chain of four linked boxes lights up one by one."},{"time":"02:45–03:00","narration":"The article gives facts. The poem gives feelings. Both say: save water!","on_screen":"Same message 💧","visual":"The article page and the poem page side by side with a tap closing between them."}],"captions_ar":["اسمع… البئر القديم يغني. عمّ تتحدث أغنيته؟","أنا البئر في الواحة القديمة…","ماذا حدث؟ هذه النتيجة. لماذا؟ هذا السبب!","يمكن لنتيجة أن تسبب الشيء التالي: سلسلة!","المقال يعطي حقائق، والقصيدة تعطي مشاعر، وكلاهما يقول: وفّر الماء!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, gentle female voice, speed 0.90. The well speaks in a deep, slow, kind voice for the poem."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Song of the Well","body":"I am the well in the old oasis, / deep in the sand where the palm trees grow. / For hundreds of years, I have waited in silence, / holding cool water in rocks far below.\n\nLong ago, camels came, thirsty and tired, / because the hot sun had burned all the day. / The travelers lowered their buckets inside me, / so they could drink and go on their way.\n\nThen came the pumps with their loud, hungry engines. / They pulled up my water both night and day. / People let taps run, and gardens were flooded, / and so my deep water slowly slipped away.\n\nNow I am lower than I have ever been. / My voice is a whisper; my heart is a drop. / Rain rarely visits; the rocks fill so slowly. / If you keep wasting, my song will stop.\n\nSo listen, dear child, when you turn on the tap: / each drop that you save is a gift to the sand. / Close it, conserve it, and share it with others, / and I will keep singing for all of this land.","word_count":174,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U2-LS3-1","genre":"poetry (original)","role":"paired","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[{"word":"silence","definition":"no sound at all","arabic":"صمت"},{"word":"lower (a bucket)","definition":"to move something down slowly","arabic":"يُنزِل (الدلو)"},{"word":"whisper","definition":"a very quiet voice","arabic":"همس"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read *The Song of the Well*. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ القصيدة واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"Who is speaking in the poem?","answer":"the well","explanation":"'I am the well…'","explanation_ar":"البئر.","options":["a camel","a child","the sun","the well"],"dok":1,"skill":"speaker","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U2-LS3-1","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where is the well?","answer":"in an old oasis","explanation":"Stanza 1.","explanation_ar":"في واحة قديمة.","options":["in a city kitchen","on a mountain","in the sea","in an old oasis"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why were the camels thirsty and tired?","answer":"because the hot sun had burned all day","explanation":"Stanza 2.","explanation_ar":"بسبب الشمس الحارة.","options":["because they ate too much","because it rained","because the hot sun had burned all day","because the well was loud"],"dok":1,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why did the travelers lower their buckets?","answer":"so they could drink","explanation":"Stanza 2.","explanation_ar":"ليشربوا.","options":["so they could drink","so they could swim","to clean the well","to make music"],"dok":1,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What pulled the water up night and day?","answer":"pumps with loud engines","explanation":"Stanza 3.","explanation_ar":"المضخات.","options":["pumps with loud engines","camels","travelers with buckets","the rain"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What will happen if people keep wasting water?","answer":"The well's song will stop.","explanation":"Stanza 4.","explanation_ar":"سيتوقف غناء البئر.","options":["The well will get bigger.","The well's song will stop.","More camels will come.","It will rain every day."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS3-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Cause and effect. Choose.","instructions_ar":"السبب والنتيجة: اختر.","items":[{"q":"*People let taps run, … and so my deep water slowly slipped away.* What is the EFFECT?","answer":"The deep water slipped away.","explanation":"After 'and so'.","explanation_ar":"النتيجة.","options":["People let taps run.","The deep water slipped away.","Gardens were green.","The well sang."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Rain rarely visits; the rocks fill so slowly.* What is the CAUSE?","answer":"Rain rarely visits.","explanation":"Little rain → slow refill.","explanation_ar":"السبب: قلة المطر.","options":["The rocks fill slowly.","Rain rarely visits.","The well is singing.","The pumps are loud."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which signal word tells you an EFFECT comes next?","answer":"so","explanation":"so → effect.","explanation_ar":"so.","options":["so","because","since","when"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words","stage":"guided"},{"q":"In the chain, what comes right after *pumps pulled up the water night and day*?","answer":"The water level went down.","explanation":"Next link.","explanation_ar":"انخفض الماء.","options":["Camels came to drink.","The well was full.","The water level went down.","It rained a lot."],"dok":2,"skill":"chain","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What does *My voice is a whisper* show about the well?","answer":"It has very little water left.","explanation":"Figurative language.","explanation_ar":"قلّ ماؤه كثيرًا.","options":["It is happy and loud.","It is full of camels.","It likes secrets.","It has very little water left."],"dok":3,"skill":"figurative language","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How are the poem and the article ALIKE?","answer":"Both say groundwater fills slowly and we must save water.","explanation":"Same message.","explanation_ar":"الرسالة نفسها.","options":["Both are told by a well.","Both rhyme.","Both say groundwater fills slowly and we must save water.","Both have headings."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS3-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Complete the Cause → Effect Chain for the poem.","instructions_ar":"أكمل سلسلة السبب ← النتيجة للقصيدة.","items":[{"q":"Link 1 – Cause: What did the pumps and the people do?","answer":"The pumps pulled up the water night and day, and people let taps run and flooded gardens.","explanation":"First cause.","explanation_ar":"السبب الأول.","dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Link 2 – Effect: What happened to the deep water?","answer":"The deep water slowly slipped away.","explanation":"Effect.","explanation_ar":"النتيجة.","dok":1,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Link 3 – Effect: How is the well now? Use words from the poem.","answer":"The well is lower than ever: 'my voice is a whisper; my heart is a drop'.","explanation":"Effect + evidence.","explanation_ar":"النتيجة + الدليل.","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Link 4 – Possible effect: What will happen if people keep wasting? Use *if … will*.","answer":"If people keep wasting water, the well will dry up and its song will stop.","explanation":"If … will.","explanation_ar":"If … will.","dok":3,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS3-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Explain and compare.","instructions_ar":"اشرح وقارن.","items":[{"q":"Write one cause and effect from the article with *so*.","answer":"Sea water is too salty to drink, so desalination plants remove the salt.","explanation":"so sentence.","explanation_ar":"جملة so.","dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Why do you think the poet lets the well speak?","answer":"To make us feel sorry for the well and care about saving water.","explanation":"Author's purpose.","explanation_ar":"هدف الكاتب.","dok":3,"skill":"author's craft","stage":"production"},{"q":"How is the poem DIFFERENT from the article?","answer":"The poem uses feelings and a speaking well; the article uses facts and headings.","explanation":"Difference.","explanation_ar":"اختلاف.","dok":3,"skill":"compare texts","stage":"production"},{"q":"What can YOU do so the well keeps singing? Write a *so* sentence.","answer":"I will turn off the tap when I brush my teeth, so less water is wasted.","explanation":"Action + so.","explanation_ar":"فعل + so.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS3-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"The Song of the Well\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “The Song of the Well”.","answer":"174 words","title":"The Song of the Well","body":"I am the well in the old oasis, / deep in the sand where the palm trees grow. / For hundreds of years, I have waited in silence, / holding cool water in rocks far below.\n\nLong ago, camels came, thirsty and tired, / because the hot sun had burned all the day. / The travelers lowered their buckets inside me, / so they could drink and go on their way.\n\nThen came the pumps with their loud, hungry engines. / They pulled up my water both night and day. / People let taps run, and gardens were flooded, / and so my deep water slowly slipped away.\n\nNow I am lower than I have ever been. / My voice is a whisper; my heart is a drop. / Rain rarely visits; the rocks fill so slowly. / If you keep wasting, my song will stop.\n\nSo listen, dear child, when you turn on the tap: / each drop that you save is a gift to the sand. / Close it, conserve it, and share it with others, / and I will keep singing for all of this land.","words":174,"limit":137}],"time_limit_sec":137},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS3-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Cause → Effect Chain","instructions":"Organizer: Write the first cause in Link 1. Each effect becomes the cause in the next link. Add the words from the poem as evidence.","items":[{"q":"Link 1 – Cause","answer":"Pumps pulled up the water night and day, and people wasted it (taps run, gardens flooded)."},{"q":"Link 2 – Effect (and new cause)","answer":"The deep water slowly slipped away (the water level went down)."},{"q":"Link 3 – Effect (and new cause)","answer":"The well is lower than ever – 'my voice is a whisper; my heart is a drop'."},{"q":"Link 4 – Possible effect","answer":"If people keep wasting water, the well will dry up – 'my song will stop'."}]}],"game":{"name":"Chain Reaction","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Chain builder: the child drags cards into a chain; each link must show a correct cause → effect. Correct links glow and water flows along the chain into a well; a wrong link breaks the chain.","Teams get a mixed pile of cause and effect cards.","They build the longest chain where each effect causes the next link.","Each link is read aloud with a signal word (so, because, as a result).","Other teams check each link.","Each correct link = 1 point; the longest correct chain = 3 bonus points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is an *effect*?","answer":"what happened","explanation":"Effect.","explanation_ar":"ما حدث.","options":["what happened","why it happened","the title","the speaker"],"dok":1,"skill":"cause and effect"},{"q":"Which signal word tells you a CAUSE comes next?","answer":"because","explanation":"because → cause.","explanation_ar":"because.","options":["because","so","as a result","then"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words"},{"q":"*The travelers lowered their buckets.* *Lowered* means ___.","answer":"moved down slowly","explanation":"Lower.","explanation_ar":"أنزلوا.","options":["threw away","lifted up","washed","moved down slowly"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"In the poem, why did the deep water slip away?","answer":"Pumps and people used too much water.","explanation":"Stanza 3.","explanation_ar":"الإفراط في الاستخدام.","options":["Pumps and people used too much water.","The camels drank it all in one day.","It turned into ice.","The well sang too loudly."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect"},{"q":"Which sentence about the camels is correct?","answer":"The camels were thirsty because the sun was hot.","explanation":"Full sentence + were.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Because the sun was hot.","The camels thirsty because sun hot.","The camels were thirsty because the sun was hot.","The camels was thirsty because the sun was hot."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"*Rain rarely visits.* *Rarely* means ___.","answer":"not often","explanation":"Rarely.","explanation_ar":"نادرًا.","options":["every day","loudly","quickly","not often"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"What is the message of *The Song of the Well*?","answer":"Save water so the well does not dry up.","explanation":"Theme.","explanation_ar":"وفّر الماء.","options":["Camels are tired animals.","Pumps are loud.","Wells are very old.","Save water so the well does not dry up."],"dok":2,"skill":"message"},{"q":"In a cause–effect chain, what does an effect become?","answer":"the cause of the next event","explanation":"Chain.","explanation_ar":"سببًا للحدث التالي.","options":["the title of the text","the cause of the next event","the last word","a question"],"dok":2,"skill":"chain"},{"q":"What fact from the article matches *the rocks fill so slowly*?","answer":"Groundwater takes thousands of years to fill up again.","explanation":"Text-to-text.","explanation_ar":"المياه الجوفية بطيئة التجدد.","options":["Riyadh gets water through pipes.","Clouds are made of drops.","Groundwater takes thousands of years to fill up again.","Al-Ahsa has palm trees."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts"},{"q":"Why is *my heart is a drop* a strong line?","answer":"It shows the well has almost no water, and it makes us feel sad.","explanation":"Figurative language.","explanation_ar":"يُظهر قلة الماء ويثير الشعور.","options":["It tells us the well has a real heart.","It shows the well has almost no water, and it makes us feel sad.","It gives a number.","It is a heading."],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'silence': a quiet desert at night"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'traveler': travelers with camels in the desert"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'bucket': a bucket on a rope"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'pump': a water pump next to a farm"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'flood': a garden covered with too much water"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'whisper': a child whispering into a friend's ear"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'rarely': a calendar with only one rainy day"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-01","prompt":"Travelers and camels drinking from an old well in an oasis."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-02","prompt":"A well with very little water, pumps, and a child closing a tap."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS3-03","prompt":"A cause-and-effect chain organizer."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V01","script":"silence. The well waited in silence."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V02","script":"traveler. The travelers stopped at the oasis."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V03","script":"bucket. He lowered the bucket into the well."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V04","script":"pump. The pump pulls water from deep under the ground."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V05","script":"flood. They flooded the garden with water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V06","script":"whisper. My voice is a whisper."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-V07","script":"rarely. Rain rarely falls in the desert."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-T1","script":"I am the well in the old oasis, / deep in the sand where the palm trees grow. / For hundreds of years, I have waited in silence, / holding cool water in rocks far below. Long ago, camels came, thirsty and tired, / because the hot sun had burned all the day. / The travelers lowered their buckets inside me, / so they could drink and go on their way. Then came the pumps with their loud, hungry engines. / They pulled up my water both night and day. / People let taps run, and gardens were flooded, / and so my deep water slowly slipped away. Now I am lower than I have ever been. / My voice is a whisper; my heart is a drop. / Rain rarely visits; the rocks fill so slowly. / If you keep wasting, my song will stop. So listen, dear child, when you turn on the tap: / each drop that you save is a gift to the sand. / Close it, conserve it, and share it with others, / and I will keep singing for all of this land."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Listen… the old well is singing. What is its song about? I am the well in the old oasis… What happened? That's the effect. Why? That's the cause! One effect can cause the next thing: a chain! The article gives facts. The poem gives feelings. Both say: save water!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS4","title":"Writing Skill: Cause–effect sentences: so, because, as a result","lesson_type":"writing_skill","objectives":["write cause–effect sentences with because, since, so, as a result and therefore","punctuate cause–effect sentences correctly (comma before so; comma after As a result)","join two short sentences into one cause–effect sentence"],"objectives_ar":["كتابة جمل سبب ونتيجة باستخدام because وsince وso وas a result وtherefore.","ترقيم جمل السبب والنتيجة بشكل صحيح.","دمج جملتين قصيرتين في جملة سبب ونتيجة واحدة."],"success_criteria":["I can choose the right signal word for a cause or an effect.","I can put commas in the right place.","I can join two sentences to show cause and effect."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع اختيار كلمة الإشارة المناسبة للسبب أو النتيجة.","أستطيع وضع الفواصل في مكانها الصحيح.","أستطيع دمج جملتين لإظهار السبب والنتيجة."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"drip","pos":"verb","ipa":"/drɪp/","definition":"to fall in small drops","arabic":"يقطر","example":"The old tap drips all night.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"leak","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/lik/","definition":"to let water out through a small hole; a small hole that lets water out","arabic":"يسرّب / تسرّب","example":"The pipe leaks under the sink.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"tightly","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈtaɪtli/","definition":"firmly, with no space","arabic":"بإحكام","example":"Close the tap tightly.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"escape","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪˈskeɪp/","definition":"to get out of a place","arabic":"يتسرّب / يهرب","example":"Water escapes from the tap.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"bill","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bɪl/","definition":"a paper that shows how much money you must pay","arabic":"فاتورة","example":"Our water bill was high this month.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"plumber","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈplʌmər/","definition":"a person whose job is to fix pipes and taps","arabic":"سبّاك","example":"The plumber fixed the tap.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"repair","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/rɪˈpɛr/","definition":"the work of fixing something; to fix","arabic":"إصلاح / يُصلح","example":"The repair took ten minutes.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"**because / since** + **cause**: *The garden flooded **because** the hose was left on.* No comma is needed when *because* is in the middle. If **because** starts the sentence, put a comma after the cause: ***Because** the hose was left on, the garden flooded.*\n\n**so** + **effect**: *The hose was left on, **so** the garden flooded.* Put a **comma before so**. **As a result,** and **Therefore,** start a **new sentence** with the effect and need a **comma**: *The hose was left on. **As a result,** the garden flooded.*\n\nTo **join two sentences**, ask: Which one is the **cause**? Which one is the **effect**? Then choose: **cause + so + effect** or **effect + because + cause**. Use **if** for a possible effect: ***If** we fix the tap, we **will** save water.*","examples":["*The camels were thirsty **because** the sun was hot.* (effect + because + cause)","***Because** the sun was hot, the camels were thirsty.* (comma after the cause)","*The sun was hot, **so** the camels were thirsty.* (cause + so + effect)","*Sea water is salty, **so** we remove the salt in desalination plants.*","*Omar took a five-minute shower. **As a result,** he saved a lot of water.*","*Groundwater fills very slowly. **Therefore,** we must not waste it.*","*Layla waters the plants in the evening **since** less water dries up when it is cool.*","***If** everyone turns off the tap while brushing, our city **will** save millions of liters.*","Join: *The pipe leaked. The floor got wet.* → ***The pipe leaked, so the floor got wet.***"],"common_errors":["✗ The tap dripped so, the bill was high. → ✓ The tap dripped, so the bill was high. (Comma **before** so.)","✗ As a result the floor got wet. → ✓ As a result, the floor got wet. (Comma **after** As a result.)","✗ Because the pipe leaked. → ✓ Because the pipe leaked, the floor got wet. (A because part alone is not a sentence.)","✗ Because the sun was hot, so the camels were thirsty. → ✓ Because the sun was hot, the camels were thirsty. (Use **because OR so**, not both.)","✗ If we will fix the tap, we save water. → ✓ If we fix the tap, we will save water. (If + present → will.)","✗ The plants died because of they had no water. → ✓ The plants died because they had no water. (because + sentence; **because of** + noun.)","✗ The bill was high so we used less water. → ✓ We used too much water, so the bill was high. (Check which is the cause!)"],"arabic":"because/since يأتي بعدهما السبب. إذا بدأت الجملة بـ because فضع فاصلة بعد جزء السبب.\n\nso يأتي بعدها النتيجة، وتوضع فاصلة قبلها. As a result, وTherefore, تبدآن جملة جديدة وتليهما فاصلة.\n\nلا تجمع because وso في جملة واحدة. وبعد because of يأتي اسم، وبعد because تأتي جملة.\n\nلدمج جملتين حدّد السبب والنتيجة ثم اختر: سبب + so + نتيجة، أو نتيجة + because + سبب."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Drip… drip… drip… Is a dripping tap a big problem? Adam found out!","on_screen":"What Happens When a Tap Drips?","visual":"A close-up of a dripping tap; a counter shows liters going up."},{"time":"00:20–01:15","narration":"A dripping tap may seem like a small problem…","on_screen":"(Adam's paragraph)","visual":"Adam in a blue wheelchair reads; signal words glow: because, so, as a result, therefore, if."},{"time":"01:15–02:00","narration":"because + cause. so + effect. Comma before so!","on_screen":"because → cause · so → effect","visual":"Two arrows: 'because' points back to the cause; 'so' points forward to the effect."},{"time":"02:00–02:40","narration":"Join two sentences: The pipe leaked. The floor got wet. → The pipe leaked, so the floor got wet.","on_screen":"Join it! 🔗","visual":"Two sentence strips click together with 'so' and a comma."},{"time":"02:40–03:00","narration":"A small repair today can save thousands of liters tomorrow!","on_screen":"Fix it, save it 🔧💧","visual":"A plumber changes a washer; the drip stops."}],"captions_ar":["تك… تك… تك… هل الصنبور الذي يقطر مشكلة كبيرة؟ آدم اكتشف ذلك!","قد يبدو الصنبور الذي يقطر مشكلة صغيرة…","because + السبب، وso + النتيجة، وفاصلة قبل so!","ادمج جملتين: تسرّب الأنبوب. ابتلّت الأرض. ← The pipe leaked, so the floor got wet.","إصلاح صغير اليوم يوفّر آلاف اللترات غدًا!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, friendly male teacher, speed 0.90. Adam reads his model paragraph."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"What Happens When a Tap Drips? (by Adam)","body":"A dripping tap may seem like a small problem, but it can waste a lot of water. When a tap is old or not closed tightly, water escapes one drop at a time. Because the drops fall all day and all night, they add up quickly. As a result, one tap that drips once every second can waste more than 10,000 liters in a year. This waste also costs money, so families pay higher water bills. In Saudi Arabia, much of our tap water comes from desalination plants, and making this water uses a lot of energy. Every wasted drop, therefore, wastes energy too. Luckily, a leaking tap is usually easy to fix, since a plumber only needs to change a small rubber part called a washer. If you hear a drip at home, tell an adult right away. A small repair today can save thousands of liters tomorrow!","word_count":150,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U2-LS4-1","genre":"model text","role":"model","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[],"annotations":["**Topic sentence:** *A dripping tap may seem like a small problem, but it can waste a lot of water.* – tells the topic and the main effect.","**because / since + cause:** *Because the drops fall all day…* / *since a plumber only needs to…* – the reason comes after the signal word.","**so + effect:** *This waste also costs money, so families pay higher water bills.* – put a **comma before so**.","**As a result, + effect:** starts a new sentence and needs a **comma** after it.","**therefore** (= so): *Every wasted drop, therefore, wastes energy too.*","**If … (then):** *If you hear a drip at home, tell an adult…* – a possible cause and what to do.","**Closing:** *A small repair today can save thousands of liters tomorrow!* – a strong final effect."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Adam's paragraph. Choose the best answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ فقرة آدم واختر أفضل إجابة.","items":[{"q":"Why does water escape from an old tap?","answer":"It is not closed tightly.","explanation":"Model text.","explanation_ar":"لأنه غير مغلق بإحكام.","options":["It is too new.","It is not closed tightly.","It is made of plastic.","It is in the garden."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How much water can a tap that drips once every second waste in a year?","answer":"more than 10,000 liters","explanation":"Model text.","explanation_ar":"أكثر من 10,000 لتر.","options":["more than 10,000 liters","one glass","about 10 liters","one bucket"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why do families pay higher bills when a tap drips?","answer":"because the waste costs money","explanation":"…so families pay higher water bills.","explanation_ar":"لأن الهدر يكلّف المال.","options":["because plumbers are expensive","because the tap is new","because the waste costs money","because of the rain"],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why does every wasted drop also waste energy, according to Adam?","answer":"Making desalinated water uses a lot of energy.","explanation":"Model text.","explanation_ar":"لأن التحلية تستهلك طاقة.","options":["Making desalinated water uses a lot of energy.","Drops are hot.","Taps need electricity.","Water is heavy."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What small part does a plumber change to stop a drip?","answer":"a washer","explanation":"Model text.","explanation_ar":"حلقة مطاطية.","options":["a pipe","a bucket","a pump","a washer"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"A person whose job is to fix pipes and taps is a ___.","answer":"plumber","explanation":"Vocabulary.","explanation_ar":"سبّاك.","options":["traveler","farmer","plumber","baker"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS4-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Signal words and commas. Choose.","instructions_ar":"كلمات الإشارة والفواصل: اختر.","items":[{"q":"*The garden flooded ___ the hose was left on.*","answer":"because","explanation":"Cause comes next.","explanation_ar":"because.","options":["because","so","as a result","therefore"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*The hose was left on, ___ the garden flooded.*","answer":"so","explanation":"Effect comes next.","explanation_ar":"so.","options":["because","so","since","if"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about the leaking pipe has the comma in the right place?","answer":"The pipe leaked, so the floor got wet.","explanation":"Comma before so.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة قبل so.","options":["The pipe leaked so, the floor got wet.","The pipe leaked, so the floor got wet.","The pipe, leaked so the floor got wet.","The pipe leaked so the floor, got wet."],"dok":1,"skill":"punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about Omar's short shower is punctuated correctly?","answer":"Omar took a short shower. As a result, he saved water.","explanation":"Comma after As a result.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Omar took a short shower. As a result he saved, water.","Omar took a short shower as, a result he saved water.","Omar took a short shower. As, a result he saved water.","Omar took a short shower. As a result, he saved water."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What is wrong with *Because the tap dripped, so the bill was high*?","answer":"It uses both because and so.","explanation":"One signal word only.","explanation_ar":"لا تجمع because وso.","options":["It has no verb.","It needs a question mark.","It is too short.","It uses both because and so."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Join: *The well was empty. The travelers were thirsty.* Which is BEST?","answer":"The well was empty, so the travelers were thirsty.","explanation":"cause + so + effect.","explanation_ar":"الأفضل.","options":["The well was empty because the travelers were thirsty.","The well was empty, as a result the travelers thirsty.","The well was empty, so the travelers were thirsty.","Because the well was empty, so the travelers were thirsty."],"dok":3,"skill":"sentence combining","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS4-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete with the word bank.","instructions_ar":"أكمل من بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"Layla turned off the tap while brushing, ________ she saved water.","answer":"so","explanation":"Effect → so.","explanation_ar":"so.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Our water bill was high ________ a pipe was leaking.","answer":"because","explanation":"Cause → because.","explanation_ar":"because.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Sami's family fixed the leaking tap. ________, they used less water.","answer":"As a result","explanation":"New sentence + comma.","explanation_ar":"As a result.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________ we water plants in the evening, less water dries up.","answer":"If","explanation":"Possible cause.","explanation_ar":"If.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Groundwater fills up very slowly. ________, we must not waste it.","answer":"Therefore","explanation":"Effect.","explanation_ar":"Therefore.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"A cactus needs little water ________ it stores water in its thick stem.","answer":"since","explanation":"Cause.","explanation_ar":"since.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS4-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write cause–effect sentences.","instructions_ar":"اكتب جمل سبب ونتيجة.","items":[{"q":"Join with *so*: *Noura left the tap on. The sink overflowed.*","answer":"Noura left the tap on, so the sink overflowed.","explanation":"so + comma.","explanation_ar":"so + فاصلة.","dok":1,"skill":"sentence combining","stage":"production"},{"q":"Join with *because*: *The plants died. Nobody watered them.*","answer":"The plants died because nobody watered them.","explanation":"because.","explanation_ar":"because.","dok":1,"skill":"sentence combining","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a sentence about saving water with *As a result,*.","answer":"We collected the water from washing vegetables. As a result, we watered the garden for free.","explanation":"As a result,","explanation_ar":"As a result,","dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write an *If … will* sentence about wasting water.","answer":"If people waste groundwater, the wells will dry up.","explanation":"If … will.","explanation_ar":"If … will.","dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Cause & Effect Dominoes","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Domino run: the child links domino tiles so each join makes a correct sentence with the right comma; when the run is complete, the dominoes fall and turn a water wheel.","Each player gets five dominoes; one domino starts in the middle.","On your turn, add a domino that makes a correct cause–effect sentence.","Read the sentence aloud; add a comma card if needed.","If you cannot play, take a domino from the pile.","The first player with no dominoes wins; each correct comma = 1 bonus point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which signal word comes before an EFFECT?","answer":"as a result","explanation":"Effect.","explanation_ar":"as a result.","options":["because","as a result","since","because of"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words"},{"q":"*The sink overflowed ___ Noura left the tap on.*","answer":"because","explanation":"Cause next.","explanation_ar":"because.","options":["so","therefore","as a result","because"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words"},{"q":"*Close the tap tightly.* *Tightly* means ___.","answer":"firmly, with no space","explanation":"Tightly.","explanation_ar":"بإحكام.","options":["firmly, with no space","slowly","loudly","a little"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Where does the comma go in *The tap dripped so the bill was high*?","answer":"before so","explanation":"Comma before so.","explanation_ar":"قبل so.","options":["after so","after The","before so","after high"],"dok":1,"skill":"punctuation"},{"q":"Which sentence about the dry garden is correct?","answer":"The plants died because they had no water.","explanation":"because + sentence.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The plants died because of they had no water.","The plants died because, they had no water.","The plants died because they had no water.","Because the plants died."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which sentence about fixing the tap is correct?","answer":"If we fix the tap, we will save water.","explanation":"If + present → will.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["If we fix the tap, we will save water.","If we will fix the tap, we save water.","If we fix the tap we saves water.","If we fixed the tap, we will saving water."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which word means the same as *so* and can start a new sentence?","answer":"Therefore,","explanation":"Therefore.","explanation_ar":"Therefore.","options":["Because,","Since,","If,","Therefore,"],"dok":2,"skill":"signal words"},{"q":"Join: *The pump broke. The farm had no water.* Which is BEST?","answer":"The pump broke, so the farm had no water.","explanation":"cause + so + effect.","explanation_ar":"الأفضل.","options":["The pump broke because the farm had no water.","The pump broke so, the farm had no water.","Because the pump broke, so the farm had no water.","The pump broke, so the farm had no water."],"dok":3,"skill":"sentence combining"},{"q":"Which sentence shows the cause and effect in the RIGHT order of logic?","answer":"We used too much water, so the bill was high.","explanation":"Cause → effect.","explanation_ar":"المنطق الصحيح.","options":["The bill was high, so we used too much water.","We used too much water, so the bill was high.","The bill was high because we paid it.","We used too much water because the bill was high."],"dok":3,"skill":"logic"},{"q":"Why does Adam end with *A small repair today can save thousands of liters tomorrow!*?","answer":"to give a strong final effect that makes readers act","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة قوية تدفع للعمل.","options":["to start a new topic","to give a strong final effect that makes readers act","to tell a story about a plumber","to ask a question"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'drip': a tap with a drop falling"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'leak': water leaking from a pipe"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'tightly': a hand closing a tap firmly"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'escape': water squeezing out of a tap"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'bill': a water bill with numbers"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'plumber': a plumber with tools under a sink"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'repair': a wrench fixing a pipe"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-01","prompt":"A dripping tap and Adam pointing at a liters counter."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-02","prompt":"Arrows showing because before a cause and so before an effect."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS4-03","prompt":"A plumber changing a washer in a tap."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V01","script":"drip. The old tap drips all night."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V02","script":"leak. The pipe leaks under the sink."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V03","script":"tightly. Close the tap tightly."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V04","script":"escape. Water escapes from the tap."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V05","script":"bill. Our water bill was high this month."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V06","script":"plumber. The plumber fixed the tap."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-V07","script":"repair. The repair took ten minutes."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-T1","script":"A dripping tap may seem like a small problem, but it can waste a lot of water. When a tap is old or not closed tightly, water escapes one drop at a time. Because the drops fall all day and all night, they add up quickly. As a result, one tap that drips once every second can waste more than 10,000 liters in a year. This waste also costs money, so families pay higher water bills. In Saudi Arabia, much of our tap water comes from desalination plants, and making this water uses a lot of energy. Every wasted drop, therefore, wastes energy too. Luckily, a leaking tap is usually easy to fix, since a plumber only needs to change a small rubber part called a washer. If you hear a drip at home, tell an adult right away. A small repair today can save thousands of liters tomorrow!"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS4-VID","script":"Drip… drip… drip… Is a dripping tap a big problem? Adam found out! A dripping tap may seem like a small problem… because + cause. so + effect. Comma before so! Join two sentences: The pipe leaked. The floor got wet. → The pipe leaked, so the floor got wet. A small repair today can save thousands of liters tomorrow!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS5","title":"Writing Workshop: Ways to Save Water at Home","lesson_type":"writing_workshop","objectives":["plan an informative paragraph about ways to save water at home with the Hamburger Plan","write 8–10 sentences that give three ways to save water and explain each one with a cause–effect sentence","revise, edit and publish a 'Water Savers' leaflet for families"],"objectives_ar":["التخطيط لفقرة معلوماتية عن طرق توفير الماء في المنزل بخطة الهامبرغر.","كتابة 8–10 جمل تعرض ثلاث طرق لتوفير الماء وتشرح كلًا منها بجملة سبب ونتيجة.","تحسين الفقرة وتدقيقها ونشرها في مطوية «موفّرو الماء» للأسر."],"success_criteria":["I can write a topic sentence that tells the main idea.","I can give three ways to save water and explain why each one works.","I can use order transitions and cause–effect signal words with correct commas."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع كتابة جملة رئيسية تُظهر الفكرة الرئيسية.","أستطيع ذكر ثلاث طرق لتوفير الماء وشرح لماذا تنجح كل منها.","أستطيع استخدام كلمات الترتيب وكلمات السبب والنتيجة بفواصل صحيحة."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"habit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhæbɪt/","definition":"something you do often, almost without thinking","arabic":"عادة","example":"Turning off the tap is a good habit.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"shower","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʃaʊər/","definition":"washing your body while standing under falling water","arabic":"دُش / استحمام بالدش","example":"A short shower saves water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"hose","pos":"noun","ipa":"/hoʊz/","definition":"a long tube that carries water","arabic":"خرطوم","example":"Don't wash the car with a hose.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"root","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rut/","definition":"the part of a plant under the ground that takes in water","arabic":"جذر","example":"Drip pipes give water to the roots.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"leaflet","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈliflɪt/","definition":"a small printed paper with information","arabic":"مطوية / نشرة","example":"We made a leaflet about saving water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"informative","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪnˈfɔrmətɪv/","definition":"giving useful facts and information","arabic":"معلوماتي","example":"An informative paragraph teaches the reader.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"collect","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈlɛkt/","definition":"to bring things together in one place","arabic":"يجمع","example":"Collect the water from the air conditioner.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"An **informative paragraph** teaches the reader **facts** about one topic. It does not tell a story, and it does not give only your opinion.\n\nUse the **Hamburger Plan**: **Top bun** – a topic sentence (the main idea). **Three layers** – three ways to save water, each with a **fact** that explains **why** it works (cause → effect). **Bottom bun** – a closing that tells the reader why it matters.\n\nJoin your ideas with **order transitions** (First, Another way is, In addition, Finally) and explain them with **signal words** (so, because, As a result, If … will). Remember the commas!","examples":["Topic sentence: ***There are many easy ways to save water at home, and every family can help.***","Way 1: ***First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth.***","Fact + effect: ***A running tap can use about six liters every minute, so this habit saves a lot of water.***","Way 2: ***Another way is to wash fruit in a bowl instead of under a running tap.***","Fact + effect: ***As a result, you can use the same water again for your plants.***","Way 3: ***In addition, water the garden in the early morning or in the evening because less water dries up in the cool air.***","Extra idea: ***Finally, collect the water from the air conditioner and use it for plants.***","Closing: ***If every family follows these steps, we will conserve our precious water for the future.***","Not informative: *Once upon a time, a drop of water lived in a tap…* (that is a story)."],"common_errors":["✗ Giving ideas with no reasons. → ✓ Add a fact: '…, so this habit saves a lot of water.' (Each way needs a **why**.)","✗ Writing about many topics (water, food, sport). → ✓ Keep to **one topic**: saving water at home. (One main idea.)","✗ First turn off the tap. → ✓ First, turn off the tap. (Comma after an order transition.)","✗ Another way is wash fruit in a bowl. → ✓ Another way is to wash fruit in a bowl. (**is to** + verb.)","✗ A running tap use six liters. → ✓ A running tap uses about six liters. (One tap → **uses**.)","✗ Copying a whole card. → ✓ Use your own words and choose three ideas. (Don't copy.)","✗ Ending with a new idea. → ✓ End with a closing that says why it matters. (Closing = big message.)"],"arabic":"الفقرة المعلوماتية تعلّم القارئ حقائق عن موضوع واحد، فلا تحكي قصة ولا تقدم رأيك فقط.\n\nخطة الهامبرغر: جملة رئيسية، ثم ثلاث طرق لتوفير الماء مع حقيقة تشرح سبب نجاح كل طريقة، ثم خاتمة تبيّن أهمية الأمر.\n\nاستخدم كلمات الترتيب (First, Another way is, In addition, Finally) وكلمات السبب والنتيجة (so, because, As a result) مع الفواصل الصحيحة.\n\nيعلّمنا الإسلام ألّا نُسرف في الماء ولو كان كثيرًا؛ اذكر ذلك إن شئت في خاتمتك."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Qatra needs your help! Let's write a paragraph that teaches families to save water.","on_screen":"Ways to Save Water at Home 💧","visual":"Qatra waves a 'Help!' sign next to a running tap."},{"time":"00:20–01:00","narration":"Read the idea cards: the bathroom, the kitchen, the garden and around the house.","on_screen":"Idea + Fact = Why it works","visual":"Four cards flip over, each showing an idea and a fact."},{"time":"01:00–01:45","narration":"Plan with the Hamburger: a topic sentence, three ways with reasons and a closing.","on_screen":"Hamburger Plan 🍔","visual":"A hamburger builds layer by layer with notes on each layer."},{"time":"01:45–02:30","narration":"First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth. A running tap can use about six liters every minute, so…","on_screen":"First, · so · As a result, · In addition,","visual":"Sentences appear on lined paper with transitions and commas highlighted."},{"time":"02:30–03:00","narration":"Revise, edit and publish your Water Savers leaflet. Every drop counts!","on_screen":"Water Savers 🏅","visual":"A folded leaflet opens; Qatra gives a gold medal."}],"captions_ar":["قطرة تحتاج مساعدتك! لنكتب فقرة تعلّم الأسر توفير الماء.","اقرأ بطاقات الأفكار: الحمّام والمطبخ والحديقة وأنحاء المنزل.","خطّط بالهامبرغر: جملة رئيسية وثلاث طرق مع أسبابها وخاتمة.","أولًا، أغلق الصنبور أثناء تنظيف أسنانك؛ فالصنبور المفتوح قد يستهلك نحو ستة لترات كل دقيقة…","حسّن ودقّق وانشر مطوية «موفّرو الماء». كل قطرة مهمة!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, cheerful female teacher, speed 0.90. Qatra the water drop helps the children."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Water-Saving Idea Cards","body":"**Card A – In the Bathroom** · Idea: turn off the tap while you brush your teeth or wash your face · Fact: a running tap can use about 6 liters of water every minute · Idea: take a short shower (about 5 minutes) instead of a full bath · Fact: a short shower uses much less water than a full bath\n\n**Card B – In the Kitchen** · Idea: fill a bowl to wash fruit and vegetables; do not wash them under a running tap · Fact: the water in the bowl can be used again to water plants · Idea: run the dishwasher only when it is full · Fact: a half-empty dishwasher uses the same amount of water as a full one\n\n**Card C – In the Garden** · Idea: water plants early in the morning or in the evening · Fact: in the cool air, less water dries up, so the roots get more · Idea: plant desert plants and use drip watering · Fact: drip pipes give water slowly, right to the roots\n\n**Card D – Around the House** · Idea: wash the car with a bucket, not a hose · Fact: a hose can use hundreds of liters; a bucket uses only a few buckets of water · Idea: collect the water that drips from the air conditioner · Fact: this clean water is good for watering plants · Remember: Islam teaches us not to waste water, even when we have a lot of it","word_count":230,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U2-LS5-1","genre":"fact cards","role":"model","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[],"annotations":["Each card gives an **idea** (what to do) and a **fact** (why it works). The fact is the **cause–effect** reason.","Choose **three ideas** from one or more cards. Explain each idea with **so, because** or **as a result**.","Use **order transitions** for an informative paragraph: **First, Another way is, In addition, Finally**."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS5-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the Water-Saving Idea Cards. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ بطاقات الأفكار واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"How much water can a running tap use every minute?","answer":"about 6 liters","explanation":"Card A.","explanation_ar":"نحو 6 لترات.","options":["about 1 liter","about 100 liters","about 6 liters","about 1,000 liters"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where should you wash fruit and vegetables to save water?","answer":"in a bowl","explanation":"Card B.","explanation_ar":"في وعاء.","options":["under a running tap","with a hose","in the shower","in a bowl"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why should you water plants early in the morning or in the evening?","answer":"In the cool air, less water dries up.","explanation":"Card C.","explanation_ar":"لأن تبخر الماء أقل.","options":["Plants sleep at noon.","The hose is cold.","In the cool air, less water dries up.","Birds drink at night."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What should you use to wash the car?","answer":"a bucket","explanation":"Card D.","explanation_ar":"دلو.","options":["a bucket","a hose","a shower","a pump"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What can you do with the water from the air conditioner?","answer":"water plants","explanation":"Card D.","explanation_ar":"سقي النباتات.","options":["drink it","water plants","throw it away","wash the car with a hose"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"When should you run the dishwasher?","answer":"only when it is full","explanation":"Card B.","explanation_ar":"عندما يكون ممتلئًا.","options":["only when it is full","after every cup","twice an hour","when it is half-empty"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS5-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Plan the paragraph. Choose.","instructions_ar":"خطّط للفقرة: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which is the BEST topic sentence for *Ways to Save Water at Home*?","answer":"There are many easy ways to save water at home, and every family can help.","explanation":"Main idea.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسية.","options":["There are many easy ways to save water at home, and every family can help.","I brushed my teeth this morning.","Water is blue and wet.","Once upon a time, there was a drop."],"dok":1,"skill":"topic sentence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence explains WHY taking a short shower saves water?","answer":"A short shower uses much less water than a full bath.","explanation":"Fact = reason.","explanation_ar":"السبب.","options":["I like showers.","A short shower uses much less water than a full bath.","Showers are in the bathroom.","My brother takes baths."],"dok":2,"skill":"reasons","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which transition introduces the SECOND way to save water?","answer":"Another way is","explanation":"Order.","explanation_ar":"Another way is.","options":["First,","Finally,","Once upon a time,","Another way is"],"dok":1,"skill":"transitions","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about watering the garden is punctuated correctly?","answer":"In addition, water the garden in the evening.","explanation":"Comma after the transition.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["In addition, water the garden in the evening.","In addition water the garden, in the evening.","In, addition water the garden in the evening.","In addition water, the garden in the evening."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which idea does NOT belong in a paragraph about saving water at home?","answer":"My favorite football team won yesterday.","explanation":"Stay on topic.","explanation_ar":"خارج الموضوع.","options":["Turn off the tap while brushing.","Wash the car with a bucket.","My favorite football team won yesterday.","Water plants in the evening."],"dok":2,"skill":"unity","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which is the strongest closing for the water-saving paragraph?","answer":"If every family follows these steps, we will conserve our water for the future.","explanation":"Why it matters.","explanation_ar":"الخاتمة الأقوى.","options":["A tap is in the kitchen.","If every family follows these steps, we will conserve our water for the future.","First, turn off the tap.","I have a blue bucket."],"dok":3,"skill":"closing","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS5-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Plan your paragraph with the Hamburger Plan.","instructions_ar":"خطط لفقرتك بخطة الهامبرغر.","items":[{"q":"Top bun – write a topic sentence about saving water at home.","answer":"There are many easy ways to save water at home, and every family can help.","explanation":"Main idea.","explanation_ar":"الفكرة الرئيسية.","dok":1,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Layer 1 – way 1 + why it works (notes).","answer":"turn off the tap while brushing – a running tap uses about 6 liters a minute","explanation":"Idea + fact.","explanation_ar":"فكرة + حقيقة.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Layers 2 and 3 – two more ways + why they work (notes).","answer":"short shower – much less water than a bath; bucket for the car – a hose uses hundreds of liters","explanation":"Two ideas + facts.","explanation_ar":"فكرتان + حقائق.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Bottom bun – write a closing that says why saving water matters.","answer":"If every family follows these steps, we will conserve our water for the future.","explanation":"Why it matters.","explanation_ar":"الأهمية.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS5-A4","type":"writing","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write, revise, edit and publish your paragraph.","instructions_ar":"اكتب فقرتك وحسّنها ودققها وانشرها.","items":[{"q":"Write your topic sentence and your first way with its reason.","answer":"There are many easy ways to save water at home. First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth. A running tap can use about six liters every minute, so this habit saves a lot of water.","explanation":"Topic + way 1.","explanation_ar":"رئيسية + طريقة 1.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write your second and third ways with their reasons.","answer":"Another way is to take a short shower because it uses much less water than a bath. In addition, wash the car with a bucket. As a result, you will not waste hundreds of liters with a hose.","explanation":"Ways 2 and 3.","explanation_ar":"الطريقتان 2 و3.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write the closing of your water-saving paragraph.","answer":"Water is precious in our country, so if every family follows these steps, we will conserve it for the future.","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write one sentence you improved after the Two-Partner Edit (before → after).","answer":"Before: First turn off the tap. After: First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth.","explanation":"Revision.","explanation_ar":"تحسين.","dok":3,"skill":"revising","stage":"production","_w":{"checklist":[],"min":null,"max":null}}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS5-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Hamburger Plan","instructions":"Organizer: Use the idea cards. Write one way to save water and its fact in each layer.","items":[{"q":"Top bun – topic sentence (main idea)","answer":"many easy ways to save water at home; every family can help"},{"q":"Layer 1 – way 1 + why it works","answer":"turn off the tap while brushing – a running tap uses about 6 liters a minute"},{"q":"Layer 2 – way 2 + why it works","answer":"wash fruit in a bowl – the water can be used again for plants"},{"q":"Layer 3 – way 3 + why it works","answer":"water the garden in the morning or evening – less water dries up"},{"q":"Bottom bun – closing (why it matters)","answer":"if every family helps, we will conserve water for the future"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U2-LS5-WR","type":"writing","instructions":"Writing: Write an informative paragraph (8–10 sentences) called 'Ways to Save Water at Home'. Give three ways to save water. Explain why each way works with so, because or as a result. End with a closing. Write an informative paragraph (8–10 sentences) called 'Ways to Save Water at Home'. Give three ways to save water. Explain why each way works with so, because or as a result. End with a closing.","instructions_ar":"اكتب فقرة معلوماتية (8–10 جمل) بعنوان «طرق توفير الماء في المنزل». اذكر ثلاث طرق لتوفير الماء، واشرح لماذا تنجح كل طريقة باستخدام so أو because أو as a result، واختم بخاتمة.","prompt":"Write an informative paragraph (8–10 sentences) called 'Ways to Save Water at Home'. Give three ways to save water. Explain why each way works with so, because or as a result. End with a closing.","checklist":["My topic sentence tells the main idea.","I gave three ways to save water at home.","I explained why each way works with so, because or as a result.","I used order transitions with commas (First, In addition, Finally).","I wrote in my own words (no copied cards).","I used the present simple correctly (a tap uses, families save).","I wrote a closing that says why saving water matters.","I checked capital letters, periods and spelling."],"rubric_id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","min_words":90,"max_words":170,"organizer":"Hamburger Plan (topic sentence – way 1 + why – way 2 + why – way 3 + why – closing)","items":[{"q":"Write an informative paragraph (8–10 sentences) called 'Ways to Save Water at Home'. Give three ways to save water. Explain why each way works with so, because or as a result. End with a closing.","answer":"There are many easy ways to save water at home, and every family can help. First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth. A running tap can use about six liters of water every minute, so this small habit saves a lot of water every day. Another way is to wash fruit and vegetables in a bowl instead of under a running tap. As a result, you can use the same water again to water your plants. In addition, water the garden early in the morning or in the evening because less water dries up in the cool air. Finally, collect the water that drips from the air conditioner and use it for plants. Water is precious in our country, and Islam teaches us not to waste it. If every family follows these steps, we will conserve our water for the future.","_w":{"checklist":["My topic sentence tells the main idea.","I gave three ways to save water at home.","I explained why each way works with so, because or as a result.","I used order transitions with commas (First, In addition, Finally).","I wrote in my own words (no copied cards).","I used the present simple correctly (a tap uses, families save).","I wrote a closing that says why saving water matters.","I checked capital letters, periods and spelling."],"min":90,"max":170}}]}],"game":{"name":"Water Savers Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Fill the tank: the child matches an idea to its fact and builds a sentence with so or because; each correct sentence adds water to the school tank. Wasteful choices (a running hose) make the tank drip.","Teams take turns picking an idea card.","They find the matching fact card.","They say the full sentence with so or because.","A correct sentence fills one level of the class water tank.","The team that adds the most levels becomes 'Water Savers of the Week'."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What does an informative paragraph do?","answer":"teaches the reader facts about one topic","explanation":"Informative.","explanation_ar":"يعلّم القارئ حقائق.","options":["tells a funny story","teaches the reader facts about one topic","gives only the writer's feelings","asks many questions"],"dok":1,"skill":"genre"},{"q":"Turning off the tap every time you brush is a good ___.","answer":"habit","explanation":"Habit.","explanation_ar":"عادة.","options":["hose","root","habit","bill"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Drip pipes give water right to the roots.* *Roots* are ___.","answer":"the parts of a plant under the ground","explanation":"Root.","explanation_ar":"جذور.","options":["the parts of a plant under the ground","the tops of trees","the leaves","the flowers"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about the running tap is correct?","answer":"A running tap uses about six liters every minute.","explanation":"One tap → uses.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["A running tap use about six liters every minute.","A running tap using about six liters every minute.","A running tap uses about six liters every minute.","A running tap are using six liters every minute."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which order is best for an informative paragraph?","answer":"topic sentence → three ways with reasons → closing","explanation":"Hamburger.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الأفضل.","options":["closing → topic sentence → ways","ways → closing → topic sentence","reasons only → topic sentence","topic sentence → three ways with reasons → closing"],"dok":1,"skill":"organization"},{"q":"Which sentence explains a water-saving idea with a cause–effect signal word?","answer":"Wash the car with a bucket, so you do not waste hundreds of liters.","explanation":"so + effect.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Wash the car with a bucket.","Wash the car with a bucket, so you do not waste hundreds of liters.","Cars are often dirty.","My car is white."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect"},{"q":"*Another way ___ to water the garden in the evening.*","answer":"is","explanation":"is to + verb.","explanation_ar":"is.","options":["are","be","being","is"],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Why should you choose only THREE ideas, not all of them?","answer":"A paragraph needs a few clear ideas with reasons, not a long list.","explanation":"Focus.","explanation_ar":"أفكار قليلة واضحة مع أسبابها.","options":["Three is a lucky number.","The cards are short.","Teachers like short work.","A paragraph needs a few clear ideas with reasons, not a long list."],"dok":3,"skill":"planning"},{"q":"Which revision makes *First turn off the tap* better?","answer":"First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth.","explanation":"Comma + detail.","explanation_ar":"التحسين الأفضل.","options":["First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth.","First turn off tap.","Turn off the tap first first.","first, turn off the tap"],"dok":2,"skill":"revising"},{"q":"Which idea would save water AND help the plants?","answer":"collecting water from the air conditioner for the garden","explanation":"Reuse.","explanation_ar":"جمع ماء المكيّف.","options":["washing the car with a hose","taking a long bath","collecting water from the air conditioner for the garden","leaving the tap on"],"dok":3,"skill":"apply"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'habit': a child turning off a tap every morning"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'shower': a shower head with water"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'hose': a green garden hose"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'root': a plant with roots under the soil"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'leaflet': a folded leaflet with water tips"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'informative': a book with a light bulb icon"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'collect': a bucket under a dripping air conditioner pipe"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-01","prompt":"A student's Water Savers leaflet with three water-saving pictures."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-02","prompt":"Four water-saving idea cards."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U2-LS5-03","prompt":"A hamburger paragraph plan."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V01","script":"habit. Turning off the tap is a good habit."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V02","script":"shower. A short shower saves water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V03","script":"hose. Don't wash the car with a hose."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V04","script":"root. Drip pipes give water to the roots."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V05","script":"leaflet. We made a leaflet about saving water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V06","script":"informative. An informative paragraph teaches the reader."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-V07","script":"collect. Collect the water from the air conditioner."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-T1","script":"**Card A – In the Bathroom** · Idea: turn off the tap while you brush your teeth or wash your face · Fact: a running tap can use about 6 liters of water every minute · Idea: take a short shower (about 5 minutes) instead of a full bath · Fact: a short shower uses much less water than a full bath **Card B – In the Kitchen** · Idea: fill a bowl to wash fruit and vegetables; do not wash them under a running tap · Fact: the water in the bowl can be used again to water plants · Idea: run the dishwasher only when it is full · Fact: a half-empty dishwasher uses the same amount of water as a full one **Card C – In the Garden** · Idea: water plants early in the morning or in the evening · Fact: in the cool air, less water dries up, so the roots get more · Idea: plant desert plants and use drip watering · Fact: drip pipes give water slowly, right to the roots **Card D – Around the House** · Idea: wash the car with a bucket, not a hose · Fact: a hose can use hundreds of liters; a bucket uses only a few buckets of water · Idea: collect the water that drips from the air conditioner · Fact: this clean water is good for watering plants · Remember: Islam teaches us not to waste water, even when we have a lot of it"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U2-LS5-VID","script":"Qatra needs your help! Let's write a paragraph that teaches families to save water. Read the idea cards: the bathroom, the kitchen, the garden and around the house. Plan with the Hamburger: a topic sentence, three ways with reasons and a closing. First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth. A running tap can use about six liters every minute, so… Revise, edit and publish your Water Savers leaflet. Every drop counts!"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Al-Ahsa has thousands of palm trees and water under the desert. It is a famous ___.","answer":"oasis","explanation":"Oasis.","explanation_ar":"واحة.","options":["river","oasis","tap","steam"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Ice cubes left on the kitchen table ___ and become water.","answer":"melt","explanation":"Heat → melt.","explanation_ar":"تذوب.","options":["freeze","flow","waste","melt"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Water rose from the boiling kettle as hot ___.","answer":"steam","explanation":"Steam.","explanation_ar":"بخار.","options":["steam","ice","groundwater","a well"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Mother keeps the meat in the ___ so it stays frozen.","answer":"freezer","explanation":"-er = machine.","explanation_ar":"الثلاجة (المجمّد).","options":["freezing","froze","freezer","freeze"],"dok":2,"skill":"word families","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which word means *use carefully so it lasts*?","answer":"conserve","explanation":"Conserve.","explanation_ar":"يرشّد.","options":["conserve","waste","flood","drip"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*The explorers followed the river for days to find where it starts.* They wanted to find its ___.","answer":"source","explanation":"Source = where it comes from.","explanation_ar":"منبعه (مصدره).","options":["result","source","cycle","bucket"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary in context","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*The water in the mountain spring was **pure**.* *Pure* means ___.","answer":"clean, with nothing else mixed in","explanation":"Pure.","explanation_ar":"نقي.","options":["very salty","frozen","hot","clean, with nothing else mixed in"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Water that lies deep under the desert in rocks and sand is called ___.","answer":"groundwater","explanation":"Groundwater.","explanation_ar":"المياه الجوفية.","options":["steam","desalination","groundwater","a drop"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*Hamza's sandals got wet ___ water was leaking from the pipe.*","answer":"because","explanation":"Cause next.","explanation_ar":"because.","options":["so","because","as a result","therefore"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence about the hot farm is punctuated correctly?","answer":"The sun was very hot, so the palms needed more water.","explanation":"Comma before so.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The sun was very hot so, the palms needed more water.","The sun, was very hot so the palms needed more water.","The sun was very hot so the palms, needed more water.","The sun was very hot, so the palms needed more water."],"dok":1,"skill":"punctuation","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Join: *The pump stopped. The palms got no water.* Which is BEST?","answer":"The pump stopped, so the palms got no water.","explanation":"cause + so + effect.","explanation_ar":"الأفضل.","options":["The pump stopped, so the palms got no water.","The pump stopped because the palms got no water.","Because the pump stopped, so the palms got no water.","The pump stopped as a result the palms got no water."],"dok":2,"skill":"sentence combining","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which is the BEST short summary of *Hamza and the Thirsty Palms*?","answer":"Hamza and Grandpa found a leaking pipe and fixed it, so the dry palms got water again.","explanation":"Main events, short.","explanation_ar":"الملخص الأفضل.","options":["Hamza and Grandpa found a leaking pipe and fixed it, so the dry palms got water again.","Hamza wore sandals on the farm.","Grandpa Saleh has a farm, a pump, a well, a pipe and many palm trees near Taif.","I think Hamza is a good detective."],"dok":3,"skill":"summarizing","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which is the BEST topic sentence for a paragraph about saving water at school?","answer":"Our school can save a lot of water in a few simple ways.","explanation":"Main idea.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسية.","options":["I like my school.","Water is wet.","Our school can save a lot of water in a few simple ways.","First, turn off the tap."],"dok":2,"skill":"topic sentence","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence does NOT belong in a paragraph about saving water at school?","answer":"Our class won the football match on Monday.","explanation":"Off topic.","explanation_ar":"لا ينتمي.","options":["Students can turn off the taps after washing their hands.","The gardener can water the plants in the evening.","We can report leaking taps to the teacher.","Our class won the football match on Monday."],"dok":1,"skill":"unity","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"}],"unit_writing":{"task":"Write an informative paragraph (8–10 sentences) called 'How Our School Can Save Water'. Give three ways to save water at school. Explain why each way works with so, because or as a result. Use order transitions and end with a closing.","model":"Our school can save a lot of water in a few simple ways. First, students should turn off the taps after they wash their hands. A running tap can waste several liters every minute, so this small habit makes a big difference. Another way is to report leaking taps and pipes to a teacher right away. A leaking tap drips all day and all night, so fixing it quickly saves thousands of liters. In addition, the gardener can water the school plants in the early morning because less water dries up in the cool air. As a result, the plants get more water and the school uses less. Water is precious in Saudi Arabia, and much of it comes from desalination plants that use a lot of energy. If everyone at school helps, we will conserve our water for the future.","marks":20}});
